# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/pools/night.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event newt_company
# en: Company for the Evening
title [36541c] = 陪客的夜晚
# en: The woman who runs the upstairs room looks you over. "The guests like good company. Laugh at the jokes, keep the glasses full, lose gracefully at cards. Nothing more: guests who want more are shown the stair. Every night is a different party, and every party pays."
text [1705cf] = 经营楼上房间的女人上下打量着你。“客人们喜欢好伙伴。笑他们的笑话，把酒杯添满，打牌时输得体面些。仅此而已——想要更多的客人，会被请下楼。每晚都是不同的聚会，每场聚会都付钱。”
# en: An upstairs room at a tavern after hours, card tables under low lamps, well-dressed guests laughing, a student in borrowed finery refilling a glass.
scene [538ab9] = 打烊后酒馆楼上的房间，低垂的灯下摆着牌桌，衣着体面的客人在笑，一个穿着借来华服的学生在添酒。
# en: Take a seat upstairs
opt.left.label [389b09] = 上楼入座
# en: Paid company, a different guest each night.
opt.left.hint [bccbb5] = 有偿陪客，每晚客人不同。
# en: She hands you a borrowed jacket that almost fits. "Smile with your eyes," she says. "The guests can tell."
opt.left.say.1 [4b634c] = 她递给你一件借来的外套，差不多合身。“用眼睛笑，”她说，“客人们分得出来。”
# en: Not tonight
opt.right.label [4bf72b] = 今晚不了
# en: "Another night, then," says the woman, writing something in a small book. You wonder what.
opt.right.say.1 [9ca2f4] = “那就改天，”那女人说着，在一个小本子上写了些什么。你很想知道她写了什么。

@event newt_company_regular
# en: The Upstairs Room
title [4e044e] = 楼上的房间
# en: {The woman who runs the upstairs room knows your face now. "There's a party tonight," she says, already holding out the jacket.|The landlady has your jacket on a peg with your name chalked above it. "Your table's waiting," she says.|"Your regulars asked after you," says the landlady, which is either flattering or a warning. Upstairs the lamps are lit.}
text [0fbd63] = {经营楼上房间的女人现在认得你了。“今晚有场聚会。”她说，外套已经递了过来。|老板娘把你的外套挂在钉子上，上方用粉笔写着你的名字。“你的桌子在等你。”她说。|“你的常客问起你了。”老板娘说，这话不知是恭维还是警告。楼上的灯已经亮了。}
# en: An upstairs room at a tavern after hours, a landlady holding out a borrowed jacket to a student at the top of the stair.
scene [4791b6] = 酒馆打烊后的楼上房间，楼梯口的老板娘把一件借来的外套递给一个学生。
# en: Work the room
opt.left.label [58bf3e] = 去招呼客人
# en: Paid company; tonight's guests decide the rest.
opt.left.hint [377aa2] = 有偿陪客；其余看今晚的客人。
# en: {You button the jacket and go up. It fits a little better than last time.|You take your jacket from its peg and climb the stair into the lamplight.|Your regulars wave you over before you've reached the top of the stair.}
opt.left.say.1 [eb8cd0] = {你扣好外套上楼。比上次合身了一点。|你从钉子上取下外套，踏着楼梯走进灯光里。|你还没走到楼梯顶，常客们就朝你招手了。}
# en: Not tonight
opt.right.label [4bf72b] = 今晚算了
# en: {"Next week, then," she says, and the jacket goes back on its peg.|She shrugs and chalks a line through tonight beside your name.|"They'll miss you," she says, and it sounds like the truth and the bill at once.}
opt.right.say.1 [3ac771] = {“那就下周。”她说，外套又挂回了钉子上。|她耸耸肩，在你名字旁边用粉笔把今晚划掉。|“他们会想你的。”她说，听着既像真话，又像账单。}

@event newt_high_table
# en: The High Table
title [06018c] = 大赌桌
# en: {Behind the upstairs room there's a back room, and in it the high table. Grisk keeps the bank. Nobody here plays for crowns alone.|The high table again. Grisk nods to you as if you were a regular. You are becoming one.|Grisk has kept your seat warm, he says. It is not a comforting thought.} {A first-year's familiar sits in a cage beside the pot.|Someone has staked a silver wand and is sweating about it.|Somebody's signed promise is in the pot, folded small.}
text [4a665f] = {楼上房间后面还有一间后屋，里面就是大赌桌。格里斯克坐庄。这里没人只为克朗下注。|又是大赌桌。格里斯克冲你点点头，就像你是熟客。你正在变成熟客。|格里斯克说他一直给你留着座位。这话可一点也不让人安心。}{一个一年级生的魔宠被关在笼子里，就放在赌注旁边。|有人押上了一根银魔杖，正在冒汗。|赌注里有一张签了名的承诺书，折得小小的。}
# en: A round table in a back room under a single green lamp, piles of coins, a goblin in a velvet waistcoat keeping the bank.
scene [f589cb] = 后屋里一张圆桌，头顶一盏绿灯，桌上堆着硬币，一个穿天鹅绒马甲的地精在坐庄。
# en: Stake your purse
opt.purse.label [6dad53] = 押上你的钱袋
# en: Guile against the table.
opt.purse.hint [8deb0b] = 诡计，对抗整张桌子。
# en: {You read the table like a book you've already finished. The pot slides over, and Grisk applauds politely with two fingers.|Your nerve holds and theirs doesn't. You walk home heavy with silver and hollow with nerves.|Somebody's folded promise is in the pot. You win it, and give it back to the owner unread. Grisk thinks that's hilarious.}
opt.purse.say.1 [65ecad] = {你把这张牌桌读得像一本早就读完的书。赌注推到了你面前，格里斯克用两根手指礼貌地鼓掌。|你的胆量撑住了，他们的没撑住。你揣着沉甸甸的银币走回家，心里却空落落的。|赌注里有一张折得小小的承诺书。你赢了，没打开就还给了它的主人。格里斯克觉得这太好笑了。}
# en: {The cards turn on you, then the room does. You leave lighter, and a prefect's lamp is going round the courtyard.|You lose the pot and your temper with it. Grisk sympathises, with interest.|You lose, and Grisk offers to take a signed promise instead of the coin you're short. You pay in coin, all of it.}
opt.purse.say.2 [6e767c] = {牌先跟你作对，接着整个房间都跟你作对。你走的时候钱袋轻了，一位级长的灯正绕着庭院转。|你输了赌注，脾气也跟着输掉了。格里斯克表示同情，连本带利。|你输了，格里斯克提出可以用一张签了名的承诺书抵你欠的钱。你付了现钱，一分不少。}
# en: Stake a favour to Grisk
opt.favour.label [7e2bea] = 押上欠格里斯克的一个人情
# en: Win big, or owe him a job.
opt.favour.hint [7556bd] = 赢一大笔，或者欠他一份差事。
# en: You stake "one favour, to be named" and win. Grisk smiles, tears up the promise, and keeps the pieces. "Next time," he says.
opt.favour.say.1 [985418] = 你押上“一个人情，日后再说”，赢了。格里斯克笑着把承诺书撕了，却把碎片收了起来。“下次吧，”他说。
# en: You lose, and Grisk folds your promise into his waistcoat pocket like a love letter. "I'll be in touch," he says. "Soon."
opt.favour.say.2 [d7a232] = 你输了，格里斯克把你的承诺书折好，像收情书一样放进马甲口袋。“我会跟你联系的，”他说，“很快。”
# en: Play the bone-dice
opt.health.label [b0d402] = 玩骨骰
# en: The old northern game. Win or bleed.
opt.health.hint [2b4c16] = 古老的北方游戏。要么赢，要么流血。
# en: The bone-dice game is played with a knife between the fingers. You keep all ten and win the pot. Grisk calls you "dear heart" for the rest of the night.
opt.health.say.1 [5a985b] = 骨骰的玩法是把刀子插在指缝之间。你十根手指一根不少，还赢了赌注。整晚格里斯克都管你叫“心肝儿”。
# en: You win the pot and lose a fair amount of skin from your left hand. Amaranth, in the morning, asks no questions, very loudly.
opt.health.say.2 [6659bd] = 你赢了赌注，左手却掉了不少皮。第二天早上，阿玛兰斯修女什么也没问，问得非常大声。
# en: Watch one hand, then go
opt.leave.label [1c61ac] = 看一局就走
# en: {You watch a student lose a familiar on a bluff, and go home and hug yours, or your pillow.|You watch, learn and leave. Grisk raises his glass to your back.|You watch a signed promise change hands across the table, and decide never to sign anything in this room.}
opt.leave.say.1 [d0582e] = {你看着一个学生在一次诈唬里输掉了自己的魔宠，回家后抱紧了你的魔宠，或者你的枕头。|你看了，学了，走了。格里斯克冲着你的背影举了举杯。|你看着一张签了名的承诺书在桌上易手，决定在这个房间里永远什么都不签。}

@event night_partner_asks
# en: Where Were You?
title [725fa7] = 你去哪儿了？
# en: {partner} is waiting on the stair with a silver token from the Gilded Newt in {their} palm. It fell out of your coat. "The upstairs room," {they} say{s}. "People talk. I'd rather hear it from you."
text [5d738c] = {partner} 在楼梯上等你，掌心里放着一枚镀金蝾螈酒馆的银筹码。它是从你外套里掉出来的。“楼上那个房间，”{they}说，“大家都在议论。我宁愿听你自己说。”
# en: Two students on a cold stone stair in the morning, one holding a tavern's silver token found in the other's coat.
scene [67e6d6] = 清晨冰冷的石阶上的两个学生，一个手里拿着从另一个外套里掉出来的酒馆银筹码。
# en: Tell {them} everything
opt.left.label [002271] = 把一切都告诉{them}
# en: You tell the truth: the glasses, the cards, the guests, the stair. {partner} is quiet a long time. "Thank you for telling me," {they} say{s} at last, and means it, and it still costs you both.
opt.left.say.1 [132cfe] = 你说了实话：酒杯、牌局、客人、楼梯。{partner} 沉默了很久。“谢谢你告诉我，”{they}终于说，是真心的，可你们俩还是都付出了代价。
# en: "It's nothing. A card game."
opt.right.label [129d58] = “没什么。就是打牌。”
# en: {partner} looks at the token, then at you, and puts it in your hand. "All right," {they} say{s}. It isn't. For a week {they} sit{s} a little further away at supper.
opt.right.say.1 [1b1621] = {partner} 看了看筹码，又看了看你，把它放回你手里。“好吧，”{they}说。并不好。接下来一个星期，晚饭时{they}都坐得离你远了一点。

@event grisk_names_favour
# en: The Favour, Named
title [44924a] = 人情，到期了
# en: Grisk is waiting in the library alcove with your promise between two fingers. "The favour," he says. "A small one. A crate goes from the boathouse to the village. Tonight. Or, if you prefer, the price of the crate." He smiles. "I always offer a choice."
text [f47834] = 格里斯克在图书馆的壁龛里等你，两根手指夹着你的承诺书。“那个人情，”他说，“很小的一个。有个箱子要从船屋运到村里。今晚。或者，你也可以付清这箱货的价钱。”他笑了。“我总是给人选择的。”
# en: A goblin in a velvet waistcoat waiting in a library alcove, a folded promise held up between two fingers.
scene [91dfbe] = 一个穿天鹅绒马甲的地精在图书馆壁龛里等着，两根手指举着一张折好的承诺书。
# en: Move the crate
opt.left.label [f1cc88] = 运箱子
# en: The crate clinks and, faintly, sings. You don't look inside. Grisk tears up your promise. "You're good at this," he says, which is the worst thing he could say.
opt.left.say.1 [eb8ddb] = 箱子叮当作响，还隐约在唱歌。你没往里看。格里斯克撕了你的承诺书。“你干这行很在行，”他说，这是他能说出的最糟的一句话。
# en: Bram stops you on the jetty and lifts the tarp. Charm-wine. The crate is gone, the favour counts as paid, and Bram has your name.
opt.left.say.2 [818fe5] = 布拉姆在码头上拦住了你，掀开了油布。是魔法酒。箱子没了，人情算是还了，布拉姆也记下了你的名字。
# en: Pay him off
opt.right.label [e88f0a] = 花钱了事
# en: You count out the crowns and Grisk gives you back the promise with a small bow. It feels like buying your own name back. It is, more or less.
opt.right.say.1 [2b02e3] = 你数出克朗，格里斯克微微鞠躬，把承诺书还给了你。感觉就像花钱买回了自己的名字。差不多就是这么回事。

@event company_birthday
# en: A Merchant's Birthday
title [da530b] = 商人的生日
# en: {A cloth merchant from the capital is sixty tonight and wants a room full of young people laughing at his stories.|The cloth merchant is back with another party. He says it's his birthday again, and nobody dares to count.|Another of the merchant's birthdays. He has started inviting his rivals, so that they can watch him be adored.} The cake is shaped like one of his ships.
text [9bcb45] = {一位从都城来的布商今晚六十岁，想要满屋子年轻人笑他的故事。|布商又来办派对了。他说今天又是他的生日，没人敢算。|又是商人的生日。他开始邀请他的对手们来，好让他们看看他有多受爱戴。}蛋糕做成了他一艘船的模样。
# en: A loud birthday party in a tavern's upstairs room, a stout merchant in a paper crown, a cake shaped like a ship.
scene [762c16] = 酒馆楼上热闹的生日聚会，一个戴纸王冠的胖商人，一块船形蛋糕。
# en: Be the life of the party
opt.left.label [365587] = 当全场的开心果
# en: Charm the room; big tips, a long night.
opt.left.hint [02f74e] = 讨满屋欢心；小费丰厚，长夜漫漫。
# en: {You laugh, sing, and dance with his aunt. He tips like a man buying a ship. You get home with the dawn and a sore throat.|He tells the story about the storm off the southern coast again, and you gasp in the right place. The tip is heavy; so are your feet.|You toast him in front of his rivals and he nearly cries. The purse he presses on you is shaped, faintly, like a ship.}
opt.left.say.1 [a808ac] = {你笑，你唱，还陪他姑妈跳了舞。他给小费的架势像在买船。你天亮才到家，嗓子也哑了。|他又讲了一遍南方海岸外那场风暴，你在该惊呼的地方惊呼。小费很沉，你的脚也很沉。|你当着他对手们的面向他敬酒，他差点哭了。他塞给你的钱袋，隐约也是船的形状。}
# en: {You laugh a moment too late at the wrong story, and he notices. A thin tip, and a long walk home past the castle's lit windows.|You call his ship by his rival's ship's name. The room goes quiet. The landlady pays you off early.|His rivals are funnier than he is, and you show it. He doesn't forgive it, and the tip says so.}
opt.left.say.2 [42906b] = {你在一个不对的故事上笑晚了一拍，他注意到了。小费很薄，回家的路很长，一路经过城堡亮着灯的窗。|你把他的船叫成了他对手的船名。满屋一片寂静。老板娘提前把你打发走了。|他的对手们比他有趣，你还表现出来了。他不肯原谅，小费也说明了这一点。}
# en: Keep the glasses full
opt.right.label [c78554] = 把酒杯添满
# en: A quiet night's pay, on your feet.
opt.right.hint [38af60] = 安静的一晚，站着挣钱。
# en: {You pour, smile and stay out of the stories. The pay is fair, and the floor is very hard.|You keep the glasses full and your mouth shut. The merchant never learns your name, which suits you.|You pour for him and his rivals alike. Nobody notices you, and you go home with honest money and sore feet.}
opt.right.say.1 [4127db] = {你倒酒，微笑，不掺和那些故事。工钱公道，地板很硬。|你把酒杯添满，嘴巴闭紧。商人始终不知道你的名字，这正合你意。|你给他和他的对手们一视同仁地倒酒。没人注意到你，你带着干净的钱和酸痛的脚回家。}

@event company_magistrate
# en: The Magistrate's Card Party
title [967495] = 地方官的牌局
# en: {A magistrate from the county court is holding a card party, and she likes to win, but not too easily.|The magistrate again. She deals you in without asking, and her eyes say she hasn't forgotten the last game.|The magistrate's party, and a new rule: whoever lets her win too obviously pays for the wine.} The landlady's look says: lose, gracefully.
text [9a23ec] = {一位郡法院的地方官在办牌局，她喜欢赢，但不喜欢赢得太容易。|又是那位地方官。她不问就给你发了牌，眼神说明她没忘记上一局。|地方官的牌局，还有一条新规矩：谁让她赢得太明显，谁就付酒钱。}老板娘的眼神说：输，要输得体面。
# en: A card table under a green lamp, a stern magistrate in a fur collar studying her hand, a student opposite her looking at the ceiling.
scene [7acc53] = 绿色灯罩下的牌桌，一位穿毛领的严肃女地方官审视着手里的牌，对面的学生望着天花板。
# en: Lose exactly enough
opt.left.label [1c11d8] = 输得恰到好处
# en: Throw the game without being seen to.
opt.left.hint [001349] = 故意输，又不被看出来。
# en: {You lose by a hair after a brave fight. She is delighted, and tips accordingly. You feel faintly like a forger.|You let her catch your bluff in the last hand. She laughs for the first time all night, and pays you twice over.|You lose so well she thinks she beat you fairly. The money is good. Lying with cards is still lying.}
opt.left.say.1 [13726b] = {你奋战一番后以毫厘之差落败。她很高兴，小费也相应丰厚。你隐约觉得自己像个造假的。|最后一手你故意让她识破你的虚张声势。她整晚头一回笑了，付了你双份。|你输得太好了，她以为自己赢得光明正大。钱不错。用牌撒谎，也还是撒谎。}
# en: {She catches you discarding an ace and puts her cards down. "Don't patronise me." Word gets about, as word from a magistrate does.|You lose too obviously, and pay for the wine, and the story of it is round the village by noon.|She sees through you in three hands and says so to the whole table. The landlady doesn't look at you on the stair.}
opt.left.say.2 [37e2f6] = {她看见你扔掉一张王牌，把牌放下。“别哄我。”消息传开了，地方官说的话总是传得开。|你输得太明显，付了酒钱，中午之前这事就传遍了全村。|三手牌她就看穿了你，还当着全桌人说了出来。下楼时老板娘没看你一眼。}
# en: Deal and keep score
opt.right.label [190c7d] = 发牌记分
# en: Honest work at the table, smaller pay.
opt.right.hint [d84b23] = 牌桌上的老实活，钱少些。
# en: {You deal, count and say nothing. It is the dullest money you've ever earned, and it's clean.|You keep the score, honestly, and she loses honestly, and doesn't tip the scorer.|You deal for four hours. The magistrate wins without help, and nods at you as if you'd had something to do with it.}
opt.right.say.1 [49cc62] = {你发牌、计分，一言不发。这是你挣过最无聊的钱，也是最干净的。|你老老实实记分，她老老实实地输，也不给记分的小费。|你发了四个小时牌。地方官不靠帮忙就赢了，朝你点点头，好像你也出了份力。}

@event company_masked
# en: The Masked Night
title [1c4157] = 假面之夜
# en: {Tonight every guest wears a mask, and nobody says why. The landlady hands you one too, plain black, no feathers.|The masks again. One guest, in lacquered silver, asks for you by the colour of your mask.|The masked night. The silver mask is here, and has saved you the seat beside it.} Without faces the room is easier to read, and harder.
text [3ef2fc] = {今晚每位客人都戴着面具，没人说为什么。老板娘也递给你一个，纯黑的，没有羽毛。|又是面具。一位戴银漆面具的客人按面具颜色点名要你。|假面之夜。银面具来了，还给你留了旁边的座位。}没有面孔，这个房间更好读懂，也更难。
# en: A candlelit upstairs room full of guests in feathered and lacquered masks, one masked figure watching a student without moving.
scene [e99bf4] = 烛光下的楼上房间，客人们戴着羽毛和漆面具，一个面具人一动不动地看着一个学生。
# en: Sit with the masks
opt.left.label [09e12b] = 陪面具客人坐
# en: The best tips, and nobody's name.
opt.left.hint [bb5065] = 小费最多，没人留名。
# en: {You learn to read a room by its hands. You go home with heavy pockets, no names, and a feeling you can't put down.|The silver mask asks you nothing at all, and tips like a duke. You lie awake wondering who that was.|Behind the masks the guests say what they mean. You come home rich and a little colder.}
opt.left.say.1 [93928e] = {你学会了从手上读懂一个房间。回家时口袋沉甸甸的，没记住一个名字，心里有种放不下的感觉。|银面具什么也没问你，打赏得像个公爵。你醒着躺了半夜，琢磨那是谁。|面具后面，客人们说的都是真心话。你回家时富了，也冷了一点。}
# en: {A masked guest won't take no for an answer, and nobody can see who it is. You leave by the back stair with a few coins and a very bad feeling.|The silver mask leans too close, and nobody else in the room seems to notice. You go home by the long way.|A guest takes your mask off, laughing, in front of everyone. Someone at the far table looks very like a prefect.}
opt.left.say.2 [163a3e] = {一位戴面具的客人不肯接受拒绝，而谁也看不见那是谁。你从后楼梯离开，带着几枚硬币和很糟的预感。|银面具凑得太近，房间里别人好像都没注意到。你绕远路回了家。|一位客人笑着当众摘了你的面具。远处桌边有个人看着很像级长。}
# en: Work the door
opt.right.label [35e80d] = 守门
# en: Fair pay in the cold stairwell.
opt.right.hint [ce08e4] = 冷楼梯间里的公道工钱。
# en: {You take coats at the door all night. The stairwell is freezing, and every coat smells of a different perfume.|You keep the door, and turn away a guest the landlady points out. The draught gets into your bones.|You work the door and watch the masks arrive one by one. The silver one bows to you, which is worse than being spoken to.}
opt.right.say.1 [e9a28c] = {你在门口收了一整晚外套。楼梯间冷得要命，每件外套都是不同的香水味。|你守着门，把老板娘指给你的一位客人挡在外面。穿堂风钻进了骨头里。|你守着门，看着面具一个个到来。银面具朝你鞠了一躬，这比跟你说话还糟。}

@event company_patron
# en: A Guest Who Offers Patronage
title [fadcec] = 想当资助人的客人
# en: {An old collector of books has asked for "the student who reads". He wants company and argument, and he says he funds promising young minds.|The old collector is back with a new pile of books and a new argument. He has been thinking about what you said, for a month.|The collector again. He calls you his protégé to the whole room now, which is flattering and a little alarming.}
text [c4b444] = {一位上了年纪的藏书家点名要“那个爱读书的学生”。他想要人陪他聊天、跟他争论，还说他资助有前途的年轻人。|老藏书家又来了，带着一摞新书和一场新争论。他把你上次说的话想了一个月。|又是那位藏书家。他现在当着满屋人叫你他的门生，既受宠若惊，又有点吓人。}
# en: An elderly scholar in a moth-eaten velvet coat at a tavern table, a pile of rare books beside a purse, talking earnestly to a student.
scene [d20e0a] = 酒馆桌边一位穿着被虫蛀过的天鹅绒外套的老学者，身旁一摞珍本书和一只钱袋，正认真地和一个学生交谈。
# en: Take the patron's purse
opt.left.label [df6446] = 收下资助人的钱
# en: Generous, and he'll want your evenings.
opt.left.hint [65b734] = 出手大方，也要占你的晚上。
# en: {He funds your books for the term, and wants you at his table every week. You argue till two, and sleep through a lecture.|The purse is generous and so is the argument, which runs until the candles do. Your coursework waits.|He pays you to disagree with him. You are good at it, and your exam reading is not getting done.}
opt.left.say.1 [4a465b] = {他资助你这学期的书，要你每周都去他桌上。你们争到两点，你睡过了一节课。|钱袋很大方，争论也很大方，一直持续到蜡烛烧完。你的功课只好等着。|他付钱让你跟他唱反调。你很擅长，可你的备考书一页也没读。}
# en: Ask to borrow his books
opt.right.label [12a896] = 请他借书给你
# en: Learning instead of money.
opt.right.hint [dabc48] = 要学问，不要钱。
# en: {He beams, and lends you three books older than the castle. You read them on the walk home by moonlight.|He lends you his annotated copy, full of furious notes in the margin. They are better than the book.|"Finally," he says, "someone who wants the books more than the money." He gives you a small purse anyway.}
opt.right.say.1 [74202e] = {他喜笑颜开，借给你三本比城堡还老的书。你借着月光在回家路上读。|他把自己的批注本借给你，页边写满了气势汹汹的笔记。比书本身还好。|“终于，”他说，“有人想要书胜过想要钱。”他还是塞给你一个小钱袋。}

@event company_castle
# en: Someone from the Castle
title [0bb5ee] = 城堡里来的人
# en: {Halfway up the stair you see {guest} at the corner table, out of robes, with a glass of wine and the air of someone who would rather not be seen either.|{guest} is at the corner table tonight. You both pretend this is a coincidence.|Tonight it is {guest} in the corner. Half the faculty seem to drink here, and there is an arrangement: nobody has seen anybody.}
text [a68b01] = {上楼走到一半，你看见{guest}坐在角落的桌边，没穿袍子，端着一杯酒，一副也不想被人看见的样子。|今晚{guest}坐在角落的桌边。你们都假装这只是巧合。|今晚角落里坐的是{guest}。似乎一半的教职员都在这儿喝酒，而且有个默契：谁也没看见谁。}
# en: A professor out of academic dress at a tavern card table, a glass of wine halfway to their mouth, looking up at a student holding a tray.
scene [eaf60e] = 一位没穿学袍的教授坐在酒馆牌桌边，酒杯举到一半，抬头看向一个端着托盘的学生。
# en: Serve {them} as if you'd never met
opt.left.label [9487b1] = 装作素不相识
# en: Discretion pays; a slip gets talked about.
opt.left.hint [d6bdb3] = 守口如瓶有赏；说漏嘴会被议论。
# en: {You serve {guest} like any guest, and {they} tip{s} like one, too generously. At breakfast {they} nod{s} to you as if nothing ever happened.|You keep a straight face all night. On the way out {guest} leaves a coin under {their} glass and, beside it, a very small nod.|Neither of you blinks. In class next week {guest} calls on you with something almost like respect.}
opt.left.say.1 [bd9acf] = {你像招呼任何客人一样招呼{guest}，{they}也像任何客人一样给了小费，给得太多。早餐时{they}朝你点点头，好像什么也没发生过。|你一整晚都绷着脸。离开时{guest}在酒杯下留了一枚硬币，旁边还有一个极轻的点头。|你们谁都没眨眼。下周课上，{guest}点你回答问题时，带着近乎尊重的神情。}
# en: {You drop a glass when {guest} looks up. Everyone turns. {guest} leaves early, and is cold to you all week.|You say "Professor" before you can stop yourself. The table laughs. {guest} does not.|{guest} catches your eye and you both flinch, in front of everyone. By morning half the village knows who was where.}
opt.left.say.2 [f2b715] = {{guest}一抬头，你就摔了一只杯子。所有人都转过头来。{guest}提前走了，一整周都对你冷冰冰的。|你没忍住叫了一声“教授”。满桌人都笑了。{guest}没笑。|{guest}和你对上眼神，你们俩当众一缩。到早上，半个村子都知道谁在哪儿了。}
# en: Slip back downstairs
opt.right.label [29770c] = 溜回楼下
# en: Give up the night's pay to stay unseen.
opt.right.hint [23a5a8] = 放弃一晚工钱，不被看见。
# en: {You give the landlady an excuse and go down the back stair. It's a lost night's pay, and the walk home is sulky.|You hand your tray to another student and leave. {guest} never sees you; your purse notices.|You go home early, and lie awake doing the sum of what you didn't earn.}
opt.right.say.1 [319f84] = {你随便找了个借口跟老板娘说，从后楼梯下去。损失了一晚工钱，回家的路走得闷闷不乐。|你把托盘交给另一个学生就走了。{guest}从没看见你；你的钱袋可注意到了。|你早早回家，躺着算你没挣到的那笔钱。}

@event company_wants_more
# en: A Guest Who Wants More
title [8893a4] = 想要更多的客人
# en: {A guest with rings on every finger has been generous all night, and now pushes a heavy purse across the table. "Come back to my inn," he says. "Just to talk." The house rule is clear.|Another guest, another heavy purse, another invitation "just to talk". The landlady is busy across the room.|You know the look now: the generous hour, then the purse, then the invitation. Tonight it comes from a woman in pearls.}
text [93c89c] = {一位每根手指都戴着戒指的客人整晚出手大方，现在把一只沉甸甸的钱袋推过桌面。“跟我回旅店吧，”他说，“就聊聊天。”店里的规矩很清楚。|又一位客人，又一只沉甸甸的钱袋，又一句“就聊聊天”。老板娘在房间另一头忙着。|你现在认得这副神情了：先是慷慨的一小时，然后是钱袋，然后是邀请。今晚开口的是一位戴珍珠的女士。}
# en: A well-dressed guest at a tavern table holding out a heavy purse, a student standing back from the table with arms folded, a landlady watching from the door.
scene [ccd9ea] = 一位衣着考究的客人在酒馆桌边递出一只沉甸甸的钱袋，一个学生抱着胳膊退开一步，老板娘在门口看着。
# en: Call the landlady
opt.left.label [5a9d9b] = 叫老板娘
# en: The house rule; the tip goes with the guest.
opt.left.hint [a788f6] = 照店规办；小费跟客人一起走。
# en: {The landlady has the guest down the stair in a minute, purse and all. You're paid for the hours, and shaky for the rest of the night.|"The stair," says the landlady, and the guest takes it. You keep your wage and lose the tip, and your hands won't stop shaking.|The guest is shown out. The landlady pours you something strong and pays you for the night. It doesn't feel like enough.}
opt.left.say.1 [f239f0] = {老板娘一分钟就把客人连人带钱袋请下了楼。你拿到了这几个钟头的工钱，剩下的整晚手都在抖。|“楼梯。”老板娘说，客人便下了楼。你保住了工钱，丢了小费，手怎么也停不下抖。|客人被请了出去。老板娘给你倒了杯烈的，付了你一整晚的钱。感觉还是不够。}
# en: Keep the purse, promise nothing
opt.right.label [06f60c] = 收下钱袋，什么也不答应
# en: Talk them round and keep it; it can go wrong.
opt.right.hint [5afeb3] = 哄住对方留下钱；可能会出岔子。
# en: {You let him believe tomorrow, and then the day after. He leaves the purse. You feel like a pickpocket with good manners.|You laugh, and keep the purse, and see the guest into a carriage, alone. It's the most you've earned in a night. You don't sleep.|You promise nothing in a way that sounds like something. She leaves happy and you leave rich, and a little ashamed.}
opt.right.say.1 [b9f14b] = {你让他以为是明天，然后是后天。他留下了钱袋。你觉得自己像个彬彬有礼的扒手。|你笑着收下钱袋，把客人送上马车，独自一人。这是你一晚挣得最多的一次。你没睡着。|你什么也没答应，却说得像答应了什么。她高高兴兴地走了，你富富裕裕地走了，还有点羞愧。}
# en: {He sees through you, and takes his purse back with a hand that grips too hard. The landlady throws him out, too late.|The guest makes a scene on the stair, loudly calling you a cheat. A prefect on the stair hears every word.|She wants the purse back, loudly, and the landlady gives it to her. You go home with nothing but a bruise on your wrist.}
opt.right.say.2 [97b13d] = {他看穿了你，一把抓回钱袋，手攥得太紧。老板娘把他轰了出去，可已经晚了。|客人在楼梯上大闹，高声骂你是骗子。楼梯上的一个级长听得一字不漏。|她大声要回钱袋，老板娘还给了她。你回家时只带着手腕上的一块淤青。}

@event newt_high_table_raise
# en: Let It Ride
title [3e70b3] = 让它接着滚
# en: {Grisk sweeps your winnings into one neat stack and pushes it back into the middle of the table. "Let it ride," he says. "The second hand pays double. Most people stop here. Most people are dull."|Grisk is already shuffling. "Again?" he says, as if it were your idea. Your winnings sit in the middle of the table, waiting.|"Second hand," says Grisk, and the players at the next table stop pretending not to watch.} The new dealer is a woman who hasn't smiled once tonight.
text [82708b] = {格里斯克把你赢的钱码成整整齐齐的一摞，又推回桌子中央。“让它接着滚，”他说，“第二手翻倍。大多数人到这儿就停了。大多数人都很无趣。”|格里斯克已经在洗牌了。“再来？”他说，好像这是你的主意。你赢的钱就摆在桌子中央，等着。|“第二手，”格里斯克说。隔壁桌的人不再假装没在看。}新来的荷官是个女人，今晚一次都没笑过。
# en: A goblin banker in a velvet waistcoat pushing a tall stack of coins back into the middle of a green-lamped card table.
scene [da05e6] = 一个穿天鹅绒马甲的地精庄家，把一大摞高高的硬币推回绿灯下牌桌的中央。
# en: Let it ride
opt.left.label [c9e833] = 让它接着滚
# en: Your winnings on one hand; the table plays harder.
opt.left.hint [23ca72] = 赢来的钱全押一手；这桌打得更狠。
# en: {The unsmiling dealer turns her last card and looks at you properly for the first time. The pot is yours, and it's heavy.|You bluff on nothing and the whole table folds. Grisk laughs so hard he has to sit down.|You win the second hand by a single card. Somewhere behind you somebody says your name, which is not ideal.}
opt.left.say.1 [e56bfa] = {不苟言笑的荷官翻开最后一张牌，第一次正眼看了你。彩池归你了，沉甸甸的。|你空手诈唬，整桌人都弃了牌。格里斯克笑得只好坐下。|你只赢了一张牌，拿下第二手。身后有人叫出了你的名字，这可不太妙。}
# en: {The dealer takes the hand without a flicker. Your winnings go back to the bank, and the walk home is very long.|You read her wrong, and she lets you know it. Grisk pats your shoulder. "That's the second hand," he says. "It's always the second hand."|The pot goes the other way. On the stair down, a lamp moves in the courtyard and you have to wait in the dark for it to pass.}
opt.left.say.2 [8c7f7e] = {荷官面不改色地吃下这一手。你赢的钱回到了庄家那里，回去的路格外漫长。|你看错了她，她也让你明白了这一点。格里斯克拍拍你的肩。“这就是第二手，”他说，“总是第二手。”|彩池去了另一边。下楼的时候，院子里有盏灯在移动，你只好在黑暗里等它过去。}
# en: Cash out
opt.right.label [62e5da] = 见好就收
# en: Walk away with what you won.
opt.right.hint [4be82b] = 带着赢来的钱走人。
# en: {You stand, pocket your winnings and bow to the table. Grisk looks almost disappointed in you.|"Dull," says Grisk fondly, as you go. Your purse doesn't think so.|You leave while the leaving is good, and whistle all the way back to the castle, very quietly.}
opt.right.say.1 [2f406e] = {你站起身，把赢的钱揣进口袋，向全桌鞠了一躬。格里斯克看上去几乎对你有点失望。|“无趣，”你离开时格里斯克亲昵地说。你的钱袋可不这么想。|你趁能走的时候走了，一路吹着口哨回城堡，吹得非常轻。}

@event newt_high_table_last
# en: Everything on One Hand
title [a24d32] = 一手定输赢
# en: {The room has gone quiet. Players from every other table have drifted over to stand around yours. Grisk takes off his rings, one by one, and sets them on the pot. "Everything," he says. "One hand. Then we see who goes home."|Grisk deals this one himself. Nobody has done that in years, someone whispers.|The whole back room is standing around your table now. Grisk rolls up his velvet sleeves.} Whatever is in the pot tonight is in it again, and more besides.
text [4c94ab] = {屋里安静了下来。别的桌的人都慢慢聚过来，围着你这桌站着。格里斯克把戒指一枚一枚摘下来，放进彩池。“全部，”他说，“一手。然后看谁回家。”|这一手由格里斯克亲自发牌。有人低声说，他已经好多年没这么做过了。|整间后屋的人都围在你这桌旁边了。格里斯克卷起了天鹅绒袖子。}今晚彩池里有的东西又都押了进来，还多了不少。
# en: A crowd of gamblers standing around one card table in a tavern back room, a goblin banker taking off his rings one by one.
scene [003020] = 酒馆后屋里，一群赌徒围着一张牌桌站着，一个地精庄家正把戒指一枚一枚摘下来。
# en: Everything on one hand
opt.left.label [6166b2] = 一手押上全部
# en: The biggest pot in the room; Grisk deals.
opt.left.hint [b65c6b] = 全屋最大的彩池；格里斯克亲自发牌。
# en: {Grisk turns his last card, looks at yours, and starts to laugh. He puts his rings back on, one by one, and pushes the pot to you. "Don't come back for a month," he says. "I mean it kindly."|You win, and the back room applauds. By morning the village has three versions of the story, and in all of them you are taller.|The whole room breathes out at once. Grisk shakes your hand with both of his. "A real player," he says, and it sounds like a warning.}
opt.left.say.1 [b90541] = {格里斯克翻开最后一张牌，看了看你的，然后笑了起来。他把戒指一枚一枚戴回去，把彩池推给你。“一个月别来了，”他说，“我是好意。”|你赢了，整间后屋都在鼓掌。到早上，村里已经有了三个版本的故事，每个版本里你都更高大一点。|整屋人同时松了一口气。格里斯克用两只手握住你的手。“真正的玩家，”他说，听着像是一句警告。}
# en: {Grisk turns a card you didn't think was left in the deck. Your stake goes back to him, a fat slice of the night's winnings with it. He's very kind about it, which is worse.|You lose the hand on one card. The crowd drifts back to their own tables as if nothing happened. On the stair, a prefect's lamp is waiting.|The pot goes to Grisk. He counts it slowly, in front of you, and offers to call you a carriage. There are no carriages.}
opt.left.say.2 [208094] = {格里斯克翻出一张你以为牌堆里早就没有的牌。你的赌注回到了他手里，还搭上今晚赢来的一大块。他对此非常客气，这更糟。|你差一张牌输了这一手。人群像什么都没发生过一样散回各自的桌子。楼梯上，一盏级长的灯正等着你。|彩池归了格里斯克。他当着你的面慢慢地数，还说要替你叫辆马车。这里根本没有马车。}
# en: Leave on a winning streak
opt.right.label [2348d4] = 趁连胜离场
# en: Two hands won, and a story to tell.
opt.right.hint [d7c45c] = 赢了两手，还多了个好故事。
# en: {You stand up in the middle of the hush. "Another night," you say, and leave with two pots in your coat. Grisk applauds, alone, and then everyone does.|You refuse the last hand. The back room is torn between booing and admiration. Your purse settles it.|"Not tonight," you say. Grisk grins all his teeth. "That," he says, "is how you get to play again."}
opt.right.say.1 [3c5c5c] = {你在一片寂静中站了起来。“改天吧，”你说，揣着两份彩池离开。格里斯克独自鼓起掌来，接着所有人都鼓起了掌。|你拒绝了最后一手。后屋的人又想喝倒彩又忍不住佩服。你的钱袋替你作了结论。|“今晚不了，”你说。格里斯克咧开满口牙笑了。“这样，”他说，“你才能下次再来玩。”}

@event company_late_hour
# en: The Second Party
title [b35304] = 第二场派对
# en: {Past two, the landlady catches your sleeve on the stair. "Another party's just come up, and I'm a pair of hands short. Same pay again."|A second party is coming up the stair as yours goes down it. The landlady looks at you and raises an eyebrow.|"One more," says the landlady, "and I'll owe you." The castle will be waking in four hours.}
text [8abd33] = {过了两点，老板娘在楼梯上拉住你的袖子。“又上来一场派对，我缺一双手。工钱照付一份。”|你这场散了往下走，第二场派对正从楼梯往上来。老板娘看着你，挑了挑眉。|“再来一场，”老板娘说，“算我欠你的。”再过四个钟头，城堡就要醒了。}
# en: A landlady catching a tired student by the sleeve on a tavern stair long after midnight, a second party arriving noisily below.
scene [a17ae4] = 午夜过后很久，老板娘在酒馆楼梯上拉住一个疲惫学生的袖子，楼下第二场派对正吵吵嚷嚷地到来。
# en: Stay till dawn
opt.left.label [2eacef] = 待到天亮
# en: Another party's pay; no sleep, and a later walk home.
opt.left.hint [5cb79d] = 再挣一场的工钱；不睡觉，回去得更晚。
# en: {You take your jacket back off the peg. The second party is louder than the first.|You splash cold water on your face and go back up. The lamps are still lit, and so are the guests.|You stay. It will be light when you get home, and the castle's early risers will see you come in.}
opt.left.say.1 [41084c] = {你又从挂钩上取下外套。第二场派对比第一场还吵。|你往脸上泼了把冷水，又回到楼上。灯还亮着，客人们也还精神着。|你留了下来。回去时天已经亮了，城堡里早起的人会看见你进门。}
# en: Go home to bed
opt.right.label [7365a0] = 回去睡觉
# en: One party is enough for one night.
opt.right.hint [88cbd4] = 一晚一场就够了。
# en: {You hand back the jacket and walk home under the last of the stars. Your bed has never been so welcome.|"Next time," you tell the landlady. You're asleep before the castle clock strikes three.|You leave the second party to someone else and sleep the four hours you have left like a stone.}
opt.right.say.1 [f92ac8] = {你交还外套，在最后几颗星星下走回去。你的床从没这么可爱过。|“下次吧，”你对老板娘说。城堡的钟还没敲三下，你就睡着了。|你把第二场派对留给别人，剩下的四个钟头睡得像块石头。}

@event company_wedding
# en: A Wedding Upstairs
title [6049bb] = 楼上的婚礼
# en: {A miller's daughter from the next valley married this afternoon, and the party has moved upstairs at the Newt to keep going.|Another wedding upstairs: a carter and a dressmaker, and both families determined to out-dance the other.|A wedding again, and the fiddler from last time, who waves at you with his bow.} The landlady wants the dancing kept going and the families kept apart.
text [0f8b0a] = {邻谷一个磨坊主的女儿今天下午出嫁，喜宴挪到了镀金蝾螈酒馆楼上接着办。|楼上又是一场婚礼：一个车夫和一个裁缝，两家人都铁了心要在跳舞上压过对方。|又是婚礼，还是上回那个提琴手，他用琴弓朝你挥了挥。}老板娘要的是舞别停，两家人别凑到一块儿。
# en: A noisy wedding party in a tavern's upstairs room, a fiddler on a table, a bride in a crooked flower crown dancing with her grandmother.
scene [995169] = 酒馆楼上一场热闹的婚宴，提琴手站在桌子上，戴着歪斜花冠的新娘正和她奶奶跳舞。
# en: Keep everyone dancing
opt.left.label [1006e1] = 让大家一直跳下去
# en: Dance with every aunt; big tips if the families mix.
opt.left.hint [61fc62] = 跟每位姑妈都跳一支；两家人要是混到一起，小费丰厚。
# en: {You dance with every aunt, two uncles and the bride. By midnight the families are singing the same song. Both fathers tip you.|You get the two grandmothers dancing together, and after that nobody can remember the feud. The tips are enormous; your feet are not.|The fiddler and you keep it going until the candles go out. You walk home with a pocket of coins and a flower in your hair.}
opt.left.say.1 [12e788] = {你跟每位姑妈、两位叔叔和新娘都跳了舞。到午夜，两家人唱起了同一首歌。两位父亲都给了你小费。|你让两位奶奶一起跳了舞，之后谁也想不起两家的过节了。小费多得惊人；你的脚可不怎么好受。|你和提琴手一直撑到蜡烛燃尽。你揣着一口袋硬币、头上插着一朵花走回去。}
# en: {You ask the wrong cousin to dance, and the families end up on opposite sides of the room. A thin tip, and a long night.|The groom's brother picks a fight with the bride's, and you're the one standing between them. The landlady pays you off early.|Nobody wants to dance with the hired help tonight. You stand by the wall for four hours.}
opt.left.say.2 [c7d730] = {你请错了表亲跳舞，两家人最后各站屋子一边。小费寥寥，长夜漫漫。|新郎的兄弟和新娘的兄弟打了起来，夹在中间的是你。老板娘提早把你打发走了。|今晚谁都不想跟雇来的帮手跳舞。你在墙边站了四个钟头。}
# en: Mind the food and the fire
opt.right.label [6d4288] = 照看吃的和炉火
# en: Steady pay, no dancing.
opt.right.hint [dfebc0] = 工钱稳当，不用跳舞。
# en: {You keep the platters full and the fire fed. Nobody notices you, which at a wedding is a kind of success.|You carry cake until your arms ache. The bride kisses your cheek on her way out, and you go home sticky and paid.|You mind the fire and watch the dancing. It's honest money, and the music is good.}
opt.right.say.1 [d3228e] = {你让盘子一直满着，炉火一直旺着。没人注意到你，在婚礼上这也算一种成功。|你端蛋糕端到胳膊发酸。新娘离开时亲了亲你的脸颊，你黏糊糊地拿着工钱回去了。|你照看着炉火，看大家跳舞。钱挣得清白，音乐也不错。}

@event company_poets
# en: The Poets' Supper
title [9664c1] = 诗人的晚宴
# en: {A society of village poets has taken the upstairs room for its supper, and needs someone to judge the contest.|{chosen(company_poets, left): The poets are back. Their president remembers your last verdict and has not forgiven it.|The poets are back. Their president remembers you pouring the wine, and asks whether you'd dare to judge this time.}|The poets' supper again, and tonight the contest is in rhyming couplets only, including the toasts.} The landlady says: whoever wins, the wine bill gets paid.
text [649eb1] = {村里的一个诗社包下了楼上的房间办晚宴，需要有人给比赛当评判。|{chosen(company_poets, left): 诗人们又来了。社长还记得你上回的裁决，至今没有原谅。|诗人们又来了。社长记得你上回给大家倒酒，问你这回敢不敢当评判。}|又是诗人的晚宴，今晚的比赛只许用押韵的对句，连祝酒词也算。}老板娘说：谁赢都行，酒钱得有人付。
# en: A long tavern table covered in wine bottles and loose manuscript pages, ink-stained poets arguing, one standing on a chair to recite.
scene [f42ab1] = 酒馆里一张长桌上摆满酒瓶和散落的手稿，满手墨迹的诗人们争论不休，有一个站在椅子上朗诵。
# en: Judge the contest
opt.left.label [478c97] = 给比赛当评判
# en: A clever verdict pleases everyone; a bad one pleases nobody.
opt.left.hint [334de3] = 裁决巧妙，人人满意；裁决糟糕，谁都不满意。
# en: {You give a prize to everyone, each for something different, and each of them thinks theirs is the real one. The wine bill gets paid with a flourish.|Your verdict, in rhyming couplets, gets a standing ovation. The president pays you himself and asks for a copy.|You find something true to say about every poem, even the long one about turnips. They tip in verse and in coin.}
opt.left.say.1 [285643] = {你给每个人都颁了奖，各有各的名目，每个人都觉得自己那个才是真的。酒钱被潇洒地付清了。|你用押韵的对句宣布裁决，全场起立鼓掌。社长亲自付了你工钱，还要了一份抄本。|你对每首诗都说出了一句真话，连那首关于萝卜的长诗也不例外。他们用诗句和硬币付小费。}
# en: {You give the prize to the poem about the president's late wife. It was, it turns out, written by her rival. The supper ends early.|Your verdict starts an argument that becomes a fight that becomes a poem about you. It is not a kind poem.|Nobody agrees with you, loudly, in couplets.}
opt.left.say.2 [058301] = {你把奖颁给了那首写社长亡妻的诗。结果那是她的对头写的。晚宴提早散了。|你的裁决引发了一场争论，争论变成了打架，打架又变成了一首写你的诗。那可不是一首客气的诗。|没人同意你，而且是大声地、用对句不同意你。}
# en: Pour and listen
opt.right.label [00550d] = 倒酒，听诗
# en: Plain pay, and a night of poems.
opt.right.hint [a684ba] = 普通的工钱，外加一晚上的诗。
# en: {You pour wine and listen to forty poems. Three of them are good, and you remember one for weeks.|You keep the glasses full and the poets talking. You go home with fair pay and a head full of rhymes.|You pour and say nothing, and learn more about metre than a term of lectures taught you.}
opt.right.say.1 [27e398] = {你一边倒酒一边听了四十首诗。有三首写得好，其中一首你记了好几个星期。|你让酒杯一直满着，让诗人们一直说着。你带着一份公道的工钱和满脑子韵脚回去了。|你只管倒酒，一言不发，学到的格律比一学期的课还多。}

@event ring_on_yourself
# en: Bet on Yourself
title [c79e66] = 押自己赢
# en: {The ring under the boathouse has a bookmaker now, with a slate. "Fancy yourself?" he says. "Put your money where your wand is. Cast what you like. Nobody down here tells."|The bookmaker knows your name and your odds, and they've shortened.|Your name is on the slate tonight before you've said you'll fight.} {flag(ring_last_standing): Across the top of his slate he has chalked LAST STANDING: step in tonight and you fight until you drop or have beaten four, or you pay the house a forfeit to walk out.|Win, and the next bout pays more.}
text [e8ea0c] = {船屋底下的擂台现在有了个庄家，拿着一块石板。“对自己有信心？”他说，“那就拿钱来证明你的魔杖。想施什么就施什么。这底下没人告密。”|庄家知道你的名字，也知道你的赔率，而且赔率变低了。|你还没说要打，石板上已经写上了你的名字。} {flag(ring_last_standing): 他在石板顶上用粉笔写着“站到最后”：今晚进场，就要一直打到倒下或连赢四场，要么就付给庄家一笔罚金退场。|赢了，下一场钱更多。}
# en: A lantern-lit cellar under a boathouse, a scorched chalk ring on wet flagstones, a bookmaker holding up a slate of odds, a crowd in scarves.
scene [435e23] = 船屋下提灯照亮的地窖，湿石板上一个烧焦的粉笔圈，庄家举着写满赔率的石板，围着围巾的人群。
# en: Bet your purse on yourself
opt.left.label [5b980a] = 把钱袋押在自己身上
# en: {You win, singed and grinning, and the bookmaker pays out through his teeth.|The crowd roars. You collect your bet and your opponent's grudging handshake.|Your name was on the slate before you agreed, and the crowd is bigger for it. You win, and the bookmaker pays you in front of all of them.}
opt.left.say.1 [19bd7d] = {你赢了，一身焦痕却咧着嘴笑，庄家咬着牙付了钱。|人群欢呼。你领了赌金，还有对手不情不愿的握手。|你还没答应，名字就上了石板，来看的人也因此更多。你赢了，庄家当着所有人的面给你付钱。}
# en: {You go down in the third exchange, and your purse goes with you. On the way home a light is on in the prefects' corridor.|A bad loss: the bet, your pride and both eyebrows.|The bigger crowd came to see you lose, it turns out. You oblige, and your purse goes with your pride.}
opt.left.say.2 [8a5511] = {第三回合你就倒下了，钱袋也跟着没了。回去的路上，级长走廊里亮着灯。|输得很惨：赌注、面子，还有两道眉毛。|原来人多是来看你输的。你如他们所愿，钱袋和面子一起交了出去。}
# en: Fight for the purse only
opt.right.label [0acb58] = 只为奖金而战
# en: {A clean win for a small purse. The money-holder asks if you'll go again.|You win and bow to your opponent. The bookmaker is already chalking your name for the next bout.|You win the purse in front of the biggest crowd yet. The bookmaker sighs at the money he didn't make on you.}
opt.right.say.1 [cddb71] = {干净利落地赢了一小笔奖金。管钱的人问你还打不打。|你赢了，向对手鞠了一躬。庄家已经在用粉笔写你下一场的名字了。|你在最多的人面前赢下了奖金。庄家为没能从你身上赚到的钱叹了口气。}
# en: {You lose, bow, and spend the walk home finding new bruises.|A loss, and the loser's purse, which is nothing at all.|You lose in front of the biggest crowd yet. At least it was only the purse.}
opt.right.say.2 [cc0e51] = {你输了，鞠了一躬，回家路上一路发现新的淤青。|输了，拿到的是输家的奖金，也就是什么都没有。|你在最多的人面前输了。至少输的只是奖金。}
# en: Not tonight
opt.no.label [4bf72b] = 今晚算了
# en: Watch, and bet if you like.
opt.no.hint [6e4615] = 在旁边看，想押就押。
# en: {The bookmaker shrugs and rubs your name off the slate.|"Your loss," says the bookmaker. "Or someone else's gain. Care to back one?"|You leave your name on the slate and your wand in your pocket.}
opt.no.say.1 [659b1f] = {庄家耸耸肩，把你的名字从石板上擦掉了。|“你的损失，”庄家说，“或者别人的收获。要押一个吗？”|你把名字留在石板上，把魔杖留在口袋里。}

@event ring_bout_2
# en: The Second Bout
title [1ddc2a] = 第二场
# en: The money-holder points at the chalk again. {~A lanky girl steps in who quit the academy last spring. She kept the wand, and the duelling stance.|A fairground conjurer steps in, still in spangles, rolling a spark across his knuckles. The crowd knows him.|A hedge-hexer from past the village steps in, a cord of knotted charms at her wrist. Some of those knots aren't legal anywhere.} {flag(ring_last_standing): Last standing: stepping out now costs a forfeit.|The purse has doubled. Or you can take what you've won and go.}
text [ab1c3c] = 管钱的学生又指了指粉笔圈。{~一个瘦高的姑娘走了进来，她去年春天退了学。魔杖她留下了，决斗的架势也留下了。|一个集市上的变戏法的走了进来，还穿着亮片衣裳，一颗火花在指节间滚来滚去。人群认得他。|一个从村子那头来的野巫走了进来，手腕上缠着一串打了结的护符。有几个结在哪儿都不合法。} {flag(ring_last_standing): 站到最后：现在退场要付罚金。|钱袋翻了一倍。或者你可以拿着赢来的钱走人。}
# en: A chalk ring under a boathouse, a fresh opponent twirling a wand, a crowd pressing in with coins in their fists.
scene [71f7ab] = 船屋下的粉笔圈，一个新对手转着魔杖，人群挤上前来，手里攥着硬币。
# en: Fight on
opt.left.label [57a906] = 接着打
# en: A harder bout, a bigger purse.
opt.left.hint [03e670] = 更难的一场，更大的钱袋。
# en: {~She duels by the book she walked out on. You've read the later chapters. Her wand ends up in the crowd, and the purse ends up heavier.|The conjurer's sparks are all show. You aim at the hand that isn't waving, and he sits down in a shower of spangles.|You cut her charm-cord with your first spell. Whatever the knots were for, it doesn't happen, and she spits and yields.}
opt.left.say.1 [3e7189] = {~她按着她丢下的那本书来决斗。可后面几章你都读过。她的魔杖飞进了人群，钱袋则沉了几分。|变戏法的火花全是花架子。你瞄准他没在挥舞的那只手，他一屁股坐进了一阵亮片雨里。|你第一道咒就斩断了她的护符绳。不管那些结是干什么用的，都没能发生，她啐了一口，认输了。}
# en: {~She was the best in her year before she left, and she still is. She helps you up off the flagstones, which is worse.|He palms a spark, and while you watch it, the other hand ends the bout. You limp up the steps with the night's winnings and singed sleeves.|One knot comes undone, and something cold walks through your head. You come round outside, with your purse, and a headache that lasts a day.}
opt.left.say.2 [6ad1eb] = {~她退学之前是她那一届最好的，现在依然是。她把你从石板上扶起来，这更让人难受。|他手心藏了一颗火花，趁你盯着它，另一只手结束了这场比试。你带着当晚的赢钱和烧焦的袖子一瘸一拐地爬上台阶。|一个结松开了，有什么冰冷的东西从你脑子里走了过去。你在外面醒来，钱袋还在，头疼了一整天。}
# en: {flag(ring_last_standing): Forfeit, and walk out|Take the purse and go}
opt.right.label [b6a8d5] = {flag(ring_last_standing): 认输，付罚金走人|拿钱走人}
# en: {flag(ring_last_standing): Last standing: the house keeps a forfeit, and the crowd remembers.|Keep what you've won.}
opt.right.hint [6b0d1c] = {flag(ring_last_standing): 站到最后：庄家扣下罚金，人群也会记住。|保住赢来的钱。}
# en: {~You bow out with the purse in your fist. The dropout shrugs and finds someone else.|You leave the conjurer to the next fool, and count your winnings on the walk home.|The hexer laughs as you go, and ties another knot.}
opt.right.say.1 [5484a9] = {~你攥着钱袋鞠躬退场。那个退学生耸耸肩，去找别人了。|你把变戏法的留给下一个傻瓜，在回去的路上数你的赢钱。|你走的时候，野巫笑了，又打了一个结。}
# en: You raise your hand and step out of the chalk. The bookmaker chalks FORFEIT across your name, takes the house's share of your purse in front of everyone, and the cellar hisses you up the stairs.
opt.right.say.2 [8cf242] = 你举起手，走出粉笔圈。庄家在你的名字上用粉笔写下“认输”，当着所有人的面从你的钱袋里拿走庄家的那份，地窖里一片嘘声把你送上楼梯。

@event ring_bout_3
# en: The Third Bout
title [7a81f9] = 第三场
# en: Two down. The cellar is packed now and the betting is loud. {~The house sends in a Conclave clerk in ink-stained cuffs, moonlighting for the purse. He reads your stance like a form.|The house sends in a prefect who lost the sash last year, and has been angry about it ever since.|The house sends in someone in a hood whose wand hand is grey to the wrist. The steps go quiet.} {flag(ring_last_standing): Last standing: the chalk, or the forfeit.|One more win and the purse is the biggest yet. Or walk away a winner.}
text [18e236] = 已经赢了两场。地窖里挤满了人，下注声震天。{~庄家派上来一个七塔议会的文书，袖口沾着墨水，为了钱袋来兼差。他读你的架势就像读一张表格。|庄家派上来一个去年被摘了绶带的级长，从那以后他一直憋着火。|庄家派上来一个戴兜帽的人，握杖的那只手一直灰到手腕。台阶上安静了。} {flag(ring_last_standing): 站到最后：要么粉笔圈，要么罚金。|再赢一场，钱袋就是今晚最大的。或者作为赢家离开。}
# en: A packed boathouse cellar roaring at a chalk ring, a wizard in a long coat stepping in, lantern light swinging.
scene [8f9042] = 挤满人的船屋地窖对着粉笔圈咆哮，一个穿长外套的巫师走进圈里，提灯的光来回摇晃。
# en: Fight on
opt.left.label [57a906] = 接着打
# en: Harder still, and worth it.
opt.left.hint [9186db] = 更难了，也更值。
# en: {~He foresees every spell you planned. So you stop planning. The clerk goes down muttering about irregular procedure, and the cellar shakes.|The ex-prefect fights like a rulebook with a grudge. You break a rule he didn't know, and the purse is fat.|The hood falls back as they go down: nobody you know, and a face older than the hands. The crowd chants your name to drown the quiet.}
opt.left.say.1 [6275cf] = {~你计划好的每一道咒他都预见到了。于是你不再计划。文书嘟囔着“程序不合规”倒下了，地窖为之震动。|前级长打起来像一本带着怨气的规章。你打破了一条他不知道的规矩，钱袋鼓鼓囊囊。|他倒下时兜帽滑落：不是你认识的人，那张脸比那双手更老。人群高喊你的名字，好压住那份寂静。}
# en: {~The clerk dismantles you, politely, by the numbers. You wake on the steps with the purse still in your pocket and a ringing ear.|The ex-prefect's ward doesn't move, and neither, after a while, do you. Your ribs remember it all week.|The hooded caster drinks something out of you that isn't blood. You go down and stay down, and someone carries you to the door.}
opt.left.say.2 [bff922] = {~文书礼貌地、按部就班地把你拆了。你在台阶上醒来，钱袋还在口袋里，耳朵嗡嗡作响。|前级长的护盾纹丝不动，过了一会儿，你也动不了了。你的肋骨记了它一整周。|兜帽施法者从你身上吸走了某种不是血的东西。你倒下就没再起来，有人把你抬到了门口。}
# en: {flag(ring_last_standing): Forfeit, and walk out|Take the purse and go}
opt.right.label [b6a8d5] = {flag(ring_last_standing): 认输，付罚金走人|拿钱走人}
# en: {flag(ring_last_standing): Last standing: the house keeps a forfeit, and the crowd remembers.|Leave a winner.}
opt.right.hint [d6d885] = {flag(ring_last_standing): 站到最后：庄家扣下罚金，人群也会记住。|赢着离开。}
# en: {~You leave the clerk waiting in the chalk with his forms. The crowd boos, and your purse doesn't care.|The ex-prefect calls you a coward. Nobody else does; you're holding too much money.|You bow to the hood and climb the steps. Some fights are better not known.}
opt.right.say.1 [ed6195] = {~你把文书和他的表格留在粉笔圈里。人群嘘你，你的钱袋才不在乎。|前级长骂你是懦夫。别人都没说；你手里的钱太多了。|你朝兜帽人鞠了一躬，爬上台阶。有些对手，还是不认识为好。}
# en: Two down, and you step out. It's a forfeit under the rules: the house takes its cut of your winnings, and the crowd, which had money on you, lets you know about it all the way to the door.
opt.right.say.2 [c95208] = 已经赢了两场，你却退场了。按规矩这算认输：庄家从你赢的钱里抽走他的那份，而押了你的人群一路把不满送到门口。

@event ring_bout_4
# en: The Last Bout
title [9d428e] = 最后一场
# en: Three down, and the cellar has gone quiet. {~The ring's own champion steps in: a duellist the academy expelled, who hasn't lost down here in a year.|The bookmaker himself takes off his coat. His wand was in it all along, and the old hands step back from the chalk.|A girl in a borrowed cloak steps in, a runaway from Thornwick. Her shadow moves a moment after she does, and the old hands start betting against you.} {flag(ring_last_standing): Last standing: win this and the night is yours.|Win, and the cellar will talk about you for a term. Or go while you can still walk.}
text [154790] = 已经赢了三场，地窖安静下来。{~擂台自己的冠军走了进来：一个被学院开除的决斗者，在这底下一年没输过。|庄家亲自脱下了外套。他的魔杖一直就在外套里，老手们从粉笔圈边退开了。|一个披着借来斗篷的姑娘走了进来，是从荆木学院跑出来的。她的影子总比她慢半拍，老手们开始押你输。} {flag(ring_last_standing): 站到最后：赢下这一场，今晚就是你的。|赢了，地窖会谈论你一整个学期。或者趁还能走的时候离开。}
# en: A boathouse cellar gone silent around a chalk ring, the night's champion stepping in, wand raised, every lantern turned toward the fighters.
scene [1fe464] = 船屋地窖在粉笔圈周围一片寂静，当晚的冠军举着魔杖走进来，所有提灯都转向了两名斗士。
# en: Fight the last bout
opt.left.label [d243fc] = 打最后一场
# en: Expert opposition; the night's whole purse.
opt.left.hint [c13a7f] = 专家级对手；今晚的全部奖金。
# en: {~The champion's ward breaks at last, and the cellar stamps until dust comes down from the boathouse floor. You go home with a purse you can barely lift.|He reads your next spell out of your head every time, so you cast the one you hadn't thought of. He goes down laughing and pays you from his own coat.|You hit the shadow, not the girl, and she yields, grinning, and buys you a drink you can't hold. You walk home sore and rich and famous in one cellar.}
opt.left.say.1 [1f47e6] = {~冠军的护盾终于破了，地窖里跺脚声震得船屋地板上的灰都落了下来。你带着一个几乎提不动的钱袋回家。|他每次都能从你脑子里读出你的下一道咒，于是你施了那道你还没想到的。他笑着倒下，从自己外套里掏钱给你。|你打的是影子，不是姑娘。她笑着认输，请你喝了一杯你端不稳的酒。你走回去时浑身酸痛，却发了财，还在一个地窖里出了名。}
# en: {~The champion ends it in one spell, and you understand why the academy wanted them gone. You wake on the steps with your night's winnings and a long walk.|The bookmaker casts things the library keeps chained, and wins clean. You crawl up the steps holding your purse and your ribs.|You can't tell the girl from her shadow, and the wrong one hits you. The crowd is so loud the prefects must hear it.}
opt.left.say.2 [6ad91d] = {~冠军一道咒就结束了比赛，你明白了学院为什么要赶走他们。你在台阶上醒来，带着当晚的赢钱，还有一段很长的路。|庄家施的是图书馆锁在链子上的那些东西，赢得干干净净。你捂着钱袋和肋骨爬上台阶。|你分不清姑娘和她的影子，结果打中你的是错的那个。人群吵得级长们一定都听见了。}
# en: {flag(ring_last_standing): Forfeit, and walk out|Take the purse and go}
opt.right.label [b6a8d5] = {flag(ring_last_standing): 认输，付罚金走人|拿钱走人}
# en: {flag(ring_last_standing): Last standing: the house keeps a forfeit, and the crowd remembers.|Three wins is a fine night.}
opt.right.hint [322c4a] = {flag(ring_last_standing): 站到最后：庄家扣下罚金，人群也会记住。|连赢三场，已经很好了。}
# en: {~You bow out with three wins and a heavy purse. The champion nods: next time.|You don't fight the man who sets the odds, and knows your thoughts. You take your winnings before he can change his mind.|You look at the runaway's shadow and decide three is plenty.}
opt.right.say.1 [5166dd] = {~你带着三场胜利和沉甸甸的钱袋鞠躬退场。冠军点点头：下次吧。|你不跟定赔率、还读得出你心思的人打。趁他改主意之前，你拿着赢钱走了。|你看了一眼那个逃学生的影子，觉得三场就够了。}
# en: You step out before the last bout. The bookmaker counts out the forfeit from your purse with great ceremony, and the cellar boos you, and a few people, quietly, look relieved for you.
opt.right.say.2 [ab9591] = 你在最后一场前退场了。庄家煞有介事地从你的钱袋里数出罚金，地窖里嘘声一片，也有几个人悄悄地替你松了口气。

@event ring_side_bets
# en: Side Bets
title [af883e] = 场边下注
# en: {You find a place on the cellar steps. The bookmaker works his way along them, slate in hand.|From the steps you can see the fighters' wand hands, which tell you more than their faces. The bookmaker is coming round.|You know the regulars on the steps now, and who bets with their heart. The bookmaker holds out his slate.}
text [f2453b] = {你在地窖台阶上找了个位置。庄家拿着石板沿台阶一路走过来。|从台阶上你能看见斗士们握杖的手，比他们的脸透露得更多。庄家过来了。|你现在认得台阶上的常客了，也知道谁是凭感情下注。庄家递出他的石板。}
# en: Students on the steps of a boathouse cellar passing coins to a bookmaker while two fighters circle in a chalk ring below.
scene [e7b110] = 船屋地窖台阶上的学生把硬币递给庄家，下面粉笔圈里两个斗士在绕圈。
# en: Back the favourite
opt.left.label [1cbc32] = 押热门
# en: A small stake on the likely winner.
opt.left.hint [8d953c] = 小注押可能的赢家。
# en: {Your fighter wins. You collect quietly and leave before anyone remembers your face.|You read the wand hands right. The bookmaker pays you as if it hurt.|The favourite wins, as favourites do. You pocket a small, sensible profit.}
opt.left.say.1 [6e3ffa] = {你押的人赢了。你悄悄领了钱，在别人记住你的脸之前就走了。|你看准了握杖的手。庄家付钱时像是很肉疼。|热门赢了，热门总是赢。你揣起一笔不大、稳妥的利润。}
# en: {Your fighter goes down in the first exchange. So does your stake.|You picked the wand hand, not the wizard. The bookmaker smiles.|The favourite slips on the wet stone, and your crowns slip with them.}
opt.left.say.2 [3062a3] = {你押的人第一回合就倒了。你的赌注也跟着倒了。|你押的是握杖的手，不是巫师。庄家笑了。|热门在湿石头上滑了一跤，你的克朗也跟着滑走了。}
# en: Back the underdog
opt.under.label [3c219b] = 押冷门
# en: A bigger stake against the odds.
opt.under.hint [e2b1d2] = 押大注，逆势而为。
# en: {The underdog wins, and you're the only one on the steps who backed them. The bookmaker counts it out very slowly.|Your long shot lands one spell, and it's enough. The steps turn round to look at you.|You saw what nobody else did, the limp in the favourite's step. You walk home heavy with silver.}
opt.under.say.1 [afce5c] = {冷门赢了，台阶上只有你押了他。庄家数钱数得特别慢。|你押的冷门打中了一道咒，一道就够了。整排台阶的人都转过头看你。|你看见了别人没看见的：热门脚下有点瘸。你揣着沉甸甸的银币回家。}
# en: {The underdog is an underdog for a reason. Your stake is gone in a minute.|A brave fight, a long fall, and your crowns go with it.|You backed your heart. Your purse pays for it.}
opt.under.say.2 [ed71ca] = {冷门之所以是冷门，是有原因的。你的赌注一分钟就没了。|一场勇敢的较量，一次重重的倒地，你的克朗也跟着去了。|你押的是你的心。你的钱袋为此买了单。}
# en: Go home
opt.home.label [c93952] = 回家
# en: {You watch one bout and go home with your purse unopened.|You leave before the bookmaker reaches you.|You climb the steps into the cold and leave the ring to its noise.}
opt.home.say.1 [37cf2b] = {你看了一场，钱袋没打开就回家了。|庄家还没走到你跟前，你就走了。|你爬上台阶走进寒夜，把擂台留给它的喧闹。}

@event ring_cameo_corvin
# en: A Familiar Grin
title [963a6b] = 熟悉的笑脸
# en: Before the next bout someone vaults the rope into the chalk: Corvin, sleeves rolled, wand spinning. He sees you and his grin slips. "Saint. Of course it's you." Then, low: "I owe three people money, and one of them has started describing what happens next. The house pays double for a grudge match. So hate me. Loudly."
text [f72f9b] = 下一场开始前，有人翻过绳子跳进了粉笔圈：科尔文，袖子卷着，魔杖在指间打转。他看见你，笑容一滑。“圣人。当然是你。”接着压低声音：“我欠三个人钱，其中一个已经开始描述接下来会发生什么了。庄家说，有私仇的比赛双倍赔。所以，恨我吧。恨得大声点。”
# en: A grinning young man vaulting a rope into a chalk ring in a lantern-lit cellar, sleeves rolled, a wand spinning in his fingers.
scene [a5617f] = 提灯照亮的地窖里，一个咧嘴笑的年轻人翻过绳子跳进粉笔圈，袖子卷着，魔杖在指间打转。
# en: Fight him for real
opt.left.label [44de8c] = 跟他真打
# en: He fights dirty, and fast.
opt.left.hint [683fb6] = 他打得又脏又快。
# en: You knock his wand into the crowd on the fifth exchange. "Rude," he says from the flagstones, and laughs, but his eyes go to the bookmaker's slate and stay there a moment too long.
opt.left.say.1 [a5e643] = 第五回合你把他的魔杖打进了人群。“真没礼貌。”他躺在石板上说，笑了起来，可他的目光落在庄家的石板上，停得久了那么一会儿。
# en: He was never where your spell landed. He hauls you up by the collar, collects his purse, and presses a few coins of it into your hand. "Your cut, for the hating. You were very convincing."
opt.left.say.2 [05451b] = 你的咒落下的地方，他从来都不在。他揪着你的领子把你拽起来，领了钱袋，往你手里塞了几枚硬币。“你的分成，算是恨我的辛苦费。你演得很像。”
# en: Put on a show, and let him win
opt.right.label [17dd33] = 演一场，让他赢
# en: {flag(ring_last_standing): Last standing: this counts as a forfeit.|Your night ends; his debt doesn't.}
opt.right.hint [9d8579] = {flag(ring_last_standing): 站到最后：这算认输。|你的夜晚结束了；他的债可没有。}
# en: You shout, he shouts, sparks fly everywhere but at each other, and you go down with a groan the back row will talk about all week. The bettors who backed you never know. Corvin does. "I owe you," he says on the steps. "Add it to the list."
opt.right.say.1 [d4399d] = 你吼，他也吼，火花朝四面八方飞，就是不往对方身上去，你倒下时那一声呻吟够后排的人谈论一整周。押你的人永远不会知道。科尔文知道。“我欠你的，”他在台阶上说，“记在账上吧。”
# en: On a last-standing night it counts as a forfeit: the bookmaker takes the house's share of your winnings on the way out.
opt.right.say.2 [f47c5f] = 在“站到最后”的夜晚，这算认输：出门时庄家从你赢的钱里抽走他的那份。

@event ring_cameo_lyra
# en: Someone Worth Losing To
title [2b98fc] = 值得输给的人
# en: The crowd parts. Lyra Vaneshade is in the chalk, gloves off, hair tied back. "So it's true." Her voice carries over the whole cellar. "You're throwing your talent away down here, in front of drunks. Fine. Then you'll lose it to someone worth losing to." Somebody is already shouting odds on House Vaneshade.
text [edf595] = 人群分开了。莱拉·凡妮希德站在粉笔圈里，手套摘了，头发扎了起来。“原来是真的。”她的声音传遍整个地窖，“你在这底下、当着一群醉鬼的面糟蹋你的天赋。好。那你就把它输给一个值得输给的人。”已经有人在喊凡妮希德家的赔率了。
# en: A proud red-haired student in a chalk ring, gloves off, hair tied back, a ribbon of flame curling from her wand, a cellar crowd roaring.
scene [2d5658] = 一个骄傲的红发学生站在粉笔圈里，摘了手套，扎起头发，一条火焰丝带从她的魔杖上卷起，地窖里的人群在咆哮。
# en: Fight her
opt.left.label [d6ea52] = 跟她打
# en: In front of everyone.
opt.left.hint [f275cb] = 当着所有人的面。
# en: Her flame breaks on your last spell and she goes down on one knee in the chalk, in front of all of them. She stands, white to the lips. "Again," she says. "In the hall. Where it counts." The crowd will be talking about it for a term.
opt.left.say.1 [c995bc] = 她的火焰撞碎在你最后一道咒上，她当着所有人的面单膝跪在了粉笔圈里。她站起来，连嘴唇都白了。“再来，”她说，“在决斗厅。在算数的地方。”人群会谈论这件事一整个学期。
# en: She takes you apart in four exchanges, beautifully. Then she walks you up the steps herself, holding your elbow. "Now you know," she says, "where you belong. It isn't here."
opt.left.say.2 [761b5d] = 她四个回合就把你拆了，漂漂亮亮。然后她亲自扶着你的胳膊把你送上台阶。“现在你知道了，”她说，“你属于哪里。不是这里。”
# en: Walk out with her
opt.right.label [e0312b] = 跟她一起走出去
# en: {flag(ring_last_standing): Last standing: this counts as a forfeit.|The crowd won't like it.}
opt.right.hint [969b9d] = {flag(ring_last_standing): 站到最后：这算认输。|人群不会喜欢的。}
# en: You step out of the chalk and offer her your arm. The cellar boos you both up the steps. Outside, in the cold, Lyra lets go of your arm and doesn't say thank you. She does walk you all the way back.
opt.right.say.1 [671a15] = 你走出粉笔圈，把胳膊递给她。整个地窖一路嘘着你们俩上了台阶。外面的寒气里，莱拉松开你的胳膊，没有说谢谢。但她一路把你送了回去。
# en: On a last-standing night it counts as a forfeit: the bookmaker takes the house's share of your winnings on the way out.
opt.right.say.2 [f47c5f] = 在“站到最后”的夜晚，这算认输：出门时庄家从你赢的钱里抽走他的那份。

@event ring_cameo_bram
# en: Out of Uniform
title [f9d558] = 没穿制服
# en: The next challenger steps in hooded, and drops the hood: Bram Hollis, without his red sash. He sees you and goes the colour of it. "You didn't see me," he says, fast and low. "I didn't see you. Nobody down here writes anything down. That's the point." Then, loud, for the crowd: "Well? Get in the chalk!"
text [efd3e1] = 下一个挑战者戴着兜帽走进来，然后摘下了兜帽：布拉姆·霍利斯，没系红绶带。他看见你，脸涨得跟绶带一个颜色。“你没看见我，”他又快又低地说，“我也没看见你。这底下没人记任何东西。这才是重点。”然后，冲着人群大声喊：“愣着干什么？进圈来！”
# en: A broad young man pulling back a hood in a chalk ring, no prefect's sash, wand gripped tight, staring at someone he didn't expect.
scene [fff819] = 一个宽肩的年轻人在粉笔圈里拉下兜帽，没系级长绶带，紧握魔杖，瞪着一个他没想到会在这里的人。
# en: Fight him
opt.left.label [b8f327] = 跟他打
# en: He hits like a wall.
opt.left.hint [a16ea6] = 他打起来像一堵墙。
# en: His ward finally gives, and he sits down hard in the chalk. Then something odd happens: he laughs, a real one, out loud. "Nobody's ever beaten me where my father couldn't hear about it," he says. He offers you his hand.
opt.left.say.1 [523938] = 他的护盾终于撑不住了，他重重坐在粉笔圈里。接着发生了一件怪事：他笑了，是真笑，笑出了声。“从来没人在我爸听不到的地方赢过我。”他说着，把手伸给了你。
# en: He walks through your spells like rain and puts you on the flagstones. On the steps he stops. "Not a word," he says. "And not a demerit either. We were never here."
opt.left.say.2 [89c6f1] = 他像走过雨一样穿过你的咒，把你放倒在石板上。在台阶上他停下来。“一个字都别说，”他说，“也不会有处分。我们从来没来过这儿。”
# en: Let him have the bout
opt.right.label [c97201] = 把这场让给他
# en: {flag(ring_last_standing): Last standing: this counts as a forfeit.|Leave him his secret, and the purse.}
opt.right.hint [ef3768] = {flag(ring_last_standing): 站到最后：这算认输。|留给他他的秘密，还有钱袋。}
# en: You step back out of the chalk and bow to him. He stares at you as if it were a trick. On the stairs to the dormitory next morning, your name isn't in his ledger, and he looks away first.
opt.right.say.1 [3f64b9] = 你退出粉笔圈，向他鞠了一躬。他瞪着你，好像这是个圈套。第二天早上在宿舍楼梯上，他的记录本里没有你的名字，而且是他先移开了目光。
# en: On a last-standing night it counts as a forfeit: the bookmaker takes the house's share of your winnings on the way out.
opt.right.say.2 [f47c5f] = 在“站到最后”的夜晚，这算认输：出门时庄家从你赢的钱里抽走他的那份。

@event ring_cameo_ilse
# en: Frost in the Chalk
title [38d938] = 粉笔圈里的霜
# en: The cellar goes cold. The lanterns shrink. A girl in white furs steps into the chalk and frost creeps out from her boots across the flagstones: Ilse Dumont. "They said the academy's best come down here," she says. She looks you over. "They lied. But you'll do."
text [9a4444] = 地窖变冷了。提灯的火苗缩了下去。一个穿白色毛皮的姑娘走进粉笔圈，霜从她的靴子边沿着石板蔓延开来：伊尔泽·杜蒙。“他们说学院最好的人会来这底下，”她说。她上下打量了你一番。“他们撒谎了。不过你也凑合。”
# en: A girl in white furs in a chalk ring, frost creeping from her boots across the flagstones, lantern flames shrinking, a crowd stepping back.
scene [5d8a80] = 一个穿白色毛皮的姑娘站在粉笔圈里，霜从她的靴子边沿着石板蔓延，提灯的火苗缩小，人群往后退。
# en: Fight her
opt.left.label [d6ea52] = 跟她打
# en: She was raised to fight.
opt.left.hint [72e00f] = 她就是被养大来战斗的。
# en: She slips on her own ice and your spell catches her before she's up. She stays down a moment, then laughs, a short Northern sound. "Again," she says. "Not tonight. But again." She takes her purse and leaves the cellar colder.
opt.left.say.1 [059246] = 她在自己的冰上滑了一下，没等她站起来，你的咒就追上了她。她在地上待了一会儿，然后笑了，一声短促的北境腔调。“再来，”她说，“不是今晚。但要再来。”她拿走她的钱袋，离开后地窖更冷了。
# en: Rime closes over your wand hand and you can't feel it to cast. She stands over you, unimpressed. "You fight like someone taught you," she says. "Find someone who didn't." Your fingers ache till morning.
opt.left.say.2 [e0c34c] = 霜封住了你握杖的手，你冻得没法施法。她站在你面前，一点也不佩服。“你打起来像是有人教过你，”她说，“去找个没被人教过的人学。”你的手指疼到了天亮。
# en: Ask her why she's down here
opt.right.label [318951] = 问她为什么来这底下
# en: {flag(ring_last_standing): Last standing: this counts as a forfeit.|Talk, and give up the night's next bout.}
opt.right.hint [8a95cf] = {flag(ring_last_standing): 站到最后：这算认输。|聊一聊，放弃今晚的下一场。}
# en: She doesn't answer. Instead she tells you your stance is wrong, then fixes it, roughly, with her boot. "Southerners," she says, as if that explained everything. The crowd boos you both, and she doesn't seem to hear.
opt.right.say.1 [a7cbb0] = 她没有回答。她反而告诉你你的站姿不对，然后用靴子粗鲁地帮你纠正了过来。“南方人。”她说，好像这就解释了一切。人群嘘你们俩，她好像根本没听见。
# en: On a last-standing night it counts as a forfeit: the bookmaker takes the house's share of your winnings on the way out.
opt.right.say.2 [f47c5f] = 在“站到最后”的夜晚，这算认输：出门时庄家从你赢的钱里抽走他的那份。

@event lyra_ring_word
# en: Lyra Has Heard
title [d959ef] = 莱拉听说了
# en: Lyra blocks the corridor. "The ring under the boathouse." She says it as if it were a smell. "Duelling for coins in a cellar, in front of drunks, with spells nobody will report. You can actually duel. I've seen you. This is beneath you." A pause. "I'd hate to lose to someone who does it."
text [3c8223] = 莱拉挡住了走廊。“船屋底下的擂台。”她说这话的样子像在说一股臭味，“在地窖里当着醉鬼的面为钱决斗，用的是没人会举报的咒语。你明明会决斗。我见过。这配不上你。”停顿了一下。“我可不想输给一个干这种事的人。”
# en: A proud red-haired student blocking a corridor with folded arms, a duelling glove tucked in her belt.
scene [437476] = 一个骄傲的红发学生双臂交叉堵在走廊上，腰带里别着一只决斗手套。
# en: "Then spar with me instead."
opt.left.label [b55172] = “那就跟我对练吧。”
# en: She stares, then almost smiles. "Tomorrow, the Duelling Hall, six sharp." She beats you, and then shows you why, which from Lyra is close to an apology for the corridor.
opt.left.say.1 [9f2ac9] = 她盯着你，然后差点笑了出来。“明天，决斗厅，六点整。”她打败了你，然后把原因指给你看，对莱拉来说，这差不多就是为走廊上的事道歉了。
# en: "It pays. You wouldn't know."
opt.right.label [140619] = “它挣钱。你不会懂的。”
# en: Her face shuts like a door. "No," she says. "I wouldn't." She walks off. Later the Newt's landlady hands back the deposit you left on your bar tab: Lyra has paid it off. That is somehow worse.
opt.right.say.1 [71f78c] = 她的脸像一扇门一样关上了。“对，”她说，“我不会懂。”她走了。后来蝾螈酒馆的老板娘把你押在酒账上的钱退给了你：莱拉替你付清了。这不知怎么更糟。

@event grisk_pickup
# en: A Parcel at the Boathouse
title [e699bb] = 船屋的包裹
# en: {Grisk is waiting on the jetty, a parcel in oilcloth under his arm. "Into the village by tomorrow afternoon. A cobbler's back door. Don't open it, don't drop it, don't be seen."|The jetty, the oilcloth, Grisk's teeth in the dark. "Same arrangement," he says.|Grisk again, and a heavier parcel than last time.} {It ticks faintly.|It's cold enough to frost your gloves.|It smells of oranges and something under the oranges.}
text [4f4a69] = {格里斯克在码头上等着，胳膊底下夹着一个油布包。“明天下午前送到村里。鞋匠铺的后门。别打开，别掉了，别被人看见。”|码头，油布包，黑暗里格里斯克的牙齿。“老规矩，”他说。|又是格里斯克，这次的包裹比上次重。}{它微微地滴答作响。|它冷得能让你的手套结霜。|它闻起来有橙子味，橙子味底下还有别的什么。}
# en: A dark boathouse jetty at midnight, a small goblin holding out a parcel wrapped in oilcloth, the lake black behind him.
scene [df2f86] = 午夜一座漆黑的船屋码头，一个小个子地精递出一个油布包裹，身后是黑沉沉的湖。
# en: Take the parcel
opt.left.label [8ea6ee] = 接下包裹
# en: {You take it. It is heavier than it looks, and the walk back to your room is very long.|You hide it under your bed. You don't sleep well with it there.|You take the heavier parcel. It smells of oranges, and under the oranges of something you decide not to name.}
opt.left.say.1 [8e3d40] = {你接了。它比看上去重，回房间的路显得特别长。|你把它藏在床底下。有它在那儿，你睡不好。|你接过了那个更沉的包裹。它有橙子的气味，橙子底下还有一种你决定不去叫出名字的气味。}
# en: Not this month
opt.right.label [9e6244] = 这个月不了
# en: {"Next month, then," says Grisk, as if it were already arranged. He tucks the parcel away. You feel watched all the way back up the lawn.|Grisk shrugs. "There's always someone." You don't like how true it sounds.|You turn down the heavier parcel. Grisk weighs it in his hand, then in his mind. "Your loss," he says. "Or not."}
opt.right.say.1 [73971d] = {“那就下个月，”格里斯克说，好像早就说定了似的。他把包裹收了起来。回草坪那头的一路上，你都觉得有人在看着你。|格里斯克耸耸肩。“总有别人的。”你不喜欢这话有多真。|你拒绝了那个更沉的包裹。格里斯克在手里掂了掂，又在心里掂了掂。“你的损失，”他说，“也许不是。”}

@event grisk_delivery
# en: The Cobbler's Back Door
title [136b0a] = 鞋匠铺的后门
# en: {~You carry Grisk's parcel down to the village in broad daylight.|Grisk's parcel, the village lane, and too many people about.|The parcel is in your satchel and the satchel is suddenly the heaviest thing you own.} Bram is at the apple stall. The cobbler's back door is past him.
text [6201ff] = {~你光天化日之下把格里斯克的包裹带进了村子。|格里斯克的包裹，村里的小巷，还有太多的人。|包裹在你的挎包里，挎包突然成了你拥有的最重的东西。}布拉姆在苹果摊前。鞋匠铺的后门就在他身后。
# en: A narrow village lane in daylight, a student with an oilcloth parcel under one arm walking past a prefect who is buying apples.
scene [8d39ee] = 白天一条狭窄的村巷，一个学生胳膊底下夹着油布包裹，正从一个买苹果的级长身边走过。
# en: Walk past as if you belong
opt.left.label [a61db7] = 若无其事地走过去
# en: {~You nod to Bram, buy an apple, and knock twice at the cobbler's door. A hand takes the parcel; another gives you a purse. Your heart takes an hour to slow down.|The door opens before you knock. Coins, a nod, done. You eat the apple on the way home and taste none of it.|The satchel feels heavier with every step past Bram. He waves. You wave. The cobbler pays, and your hands shake until supper.}
opt.left.say.1 [3b834c] = {~你冲布拉姆点点头，买了个苹果，在鞋匠铺的门上敲了两下。一只手接过包裹，另一只手递给你一个钱袋。你的心跳过了一个钟头才慢下来。|你还没敲门，门就开了。硬币，点头，完事。你在回家路上吃了那个苹果，一点味道也没尝出来。|从布拉姆身边走过，挎包每一步都更沉。他挥手，你也挥手。鞋匠付了钱，你的手一直抖到晚饭。}
# en: {~Bram calls your name. You drop the parcel in a horse trough and walk on, very calmly. Bram follows you halfway home.|You panic at the corner and leave the parcel behind a water butt. When you go back, it's gone, and Bram is writing in his notebook.|Bram asks to see inside your satchel, kindly. You show him your books, and he never looks in the other pocket. You walk home sick.}
opt.left.say.2 [82c22c] = {~布拉姆叫了你的名字。你把包裹扔进饮马槽，非常镇定地继续走。布拉姆跟了你半路。|你在拐角处慌了神，把包裹丢在了一个水桶后面。等你回去找，它已经不见了，布拉姆正在本子上写着什么。|布拉姆客气地要看看你的挎包。你给他看了书，他始终没看另一个口袋。你走回家时一阵恶心。}
# en: Leave it at the door and run
opt.right.label [44439b] = 丢在门口就跑
# en: {~You go the long way round, drop it on the cobbler's step and run. The cobbler pays you, short, for the lack of manners.|You don't knock, and you don't wait. Short pay, slipped under your door that night.|You drop the satchel's weight on the cobbler's step and run. He pays you short, and you're glad to be rid of it.}
opt.right.say.1 [e7e8e0] = {~你绕远路，把它丢在鞋匠铺门口的台阶上就跑。鞋匠因为你没礼貌，少付了你一些钱。|你不敲门，也不等。那天夜里，一份打了折扣的报酬从你门缝底下塞了进来。|你把挎包里的东西丢在鞋匠的台阶上就跑。他少付了你钱，你却庆幸终于甩掉了它。}

@event grisk_cross
# en: Grisk Is Not Pleased
title [2bad70] = 格里斯克不高兴了
# en: Grisk is sitting on your bed. You didn't leave the window open. "A parcel was lost," he says pleasantly, turning a page in his ledger. "Lost things have a price. I've written it down. Would you like to see?"
text [ecab8b] = 格里斯克坐在你的床上。你没有开窗。“一个包裹丢了，”他愉快地说，翻着账簿。“丢了的东西是有价钱的。我已经记下来了。要看看吗？”
# en: A goblin in a velvet waistcoat sitting on a student's bed uninvited, a ledger open on his knee, the dormitory window open behind him.
scene [e93020] = 一个穿天鹅绒马甲的地精不请自来地坐在学生床上，膝上摊着账簿，身后宿舍的窗户开着。
# en: Put it on your account
opt.left.label [e01cc0] = 记在你的账上
# en: "Two more months," he says, and writes it neatly. "Such a good customer." He leaves by the window. You don't sleep with it open again.
opt.left.say.1 [aa63e2] = “再加两个月，”他说着，把它写得整整齐齐。“真是个好主顾。”他从窗户走了。从那以后你再也没开着窗睡过觉。
# en: He writes your name in the ledger under a new line: one parcel, six payments. "Twelve a month," he says, "as usual." He leaves by the window. You don't sleep with it open again.
opt.left.say.2 [0b39d1] = 他在账簿上你的名字下面新添了一行：一个包裹，分六期。“每月十二克朗，”他说，“老规矩。”他从窗户走了。从那以后你再也没开着窗睡过觉。
# en: Tell him you're done
opt.right.label [1b5f57] = 告诉他你不干了
# en: "Everyone is, eventually," Grisk says. On your way to breakfast, the stair you always take collapses three steps under you. Nobody saw. Everybody heard. You never see him again.
opt.right.say.1 [1693f0] = “每个人最后都会这么说，”格里斯克说。去吃早饭的路上，你常走的那段楼梯在你脚下塌了三级。没人看见。所有人都听见了。你再也没见过他。

@event kitchen_stores
# en: The Stores
title [de5442] = 储藏室
# en: {Behind the kitchens is the storeroom, full of sugar, spices and oranges from the south. The village pays well for oranges in winter, and nobody counts the crates.|The storeroom again. You know which crate is at the back and never counted.|The stores have a new padlock, which is mostly decorative.} {A mouse watches you without judgement.|The kitchen cat does judge you.|Somewhere a pot is still dripping.}
text [855855] = {厨房后面是储藏室，堆满了糖、香料和南方运来的橙子。冬天村里橙子卖得好，而且没人清点这些箱子。|又是储藏室。你知道哪一箱在最里面，从来没人数过。|储藏室换了一把新挂锁，基本上是个摆设。}{一只老鼠看着你，毫无评判之意。|厨房的猫倒是在评判你。|某处一口锅还在滴水。}
# en: A dark storeroom behind a castle kitchen, sacks of sugar and crates of oranges stacked high, a student with an empty satchel.
scene [6082df] = 城堡厨房后面一间漆黑的储藏室，糖袋和橙子箱堆得老高，一个学生拿着空挎包。
# en: Fill a satchel to sell
opt.left.label [d756fa] = 装满一挎包去卖
# en: {Oranges, a cone of sugar, a jar of saffron. The village grocer asks no questions and pays in coppers. Somebody in the castle will be short of saffron.|A full satchel and an empty conscience, or nearly. On the way out, the scullery door bangs behind you.|The new padlock opens with a hairpin. You fill the satchel, and the grocer pays, and you wonder who'll be blamed for the lock.}
opt.left.say.1 [43fa37] = {橙子、一块圆锥形的糖、一罐藏红花。村里的杂货商什么也不问，付的是铜板。城堡里会有人缺藏红花用了。|挎包装满了，良心几乎清空了。出门时，洗碗间的门在你身后砰的一响。|新挂锁用一根发夹就开了。你装满了挎包，杂货商付了钱，你想知道这锁的事会怪到谁头上。}
# en: Take one orange and go
opt.right.label [1f5959] = 拿一个橙子就走
# en: {You eat it in the dark by the banked fire. It's the best orange you have ever eaten, and you know exactly why.|One orange. You leave the peel in the fire so nobody finds it.|You take one orange past the new padlock and feel worse about it than about all the crates.}
opt.right.say.1 [4f7fd6] = {你在黑暗中靠着封住的炉火把它吃了。这是你吃过最好吃的橙子，你也很清楚为什么。|一个橙子。你把皮丢进火里，这样没人会发现。|你绕过新挂锁拿了一个橙子，感觉比偷了所有箱子还糟。}

@event kitchen_night_baker
# en: The Night Baker
title [97e00b] = 守夜的面包师
# en: {The bakehouse behind the kitchens is lit. The night baker, flour to the elbows, looks up. "Hungry or helpful?" she says. "Both is allowed."|The night baker waves you in without looking up. "Dough's waiting."|The bakehouse smells of tomorrow's bread. The baker has saved you a heel of yesterday's.} {The oven sighs.|A tray of rolls is cooling by the door.|She is humming something old.}
text [1b7271] = {厨房后面的烤房亮着灯。守夜的面包师手臂上沾满面粉，抬起头来。“饿了还是来帮忙？”她说，“两样都行。”|守夜的面包师头也不抬地招手让你进来。“面团在等你。”|烤房里飘着明天的面包香。面包师给你留了一块昨天的面包头。}{炉子叹了口气。|一盘小面包正在门边晾着。|她在哼一支古老的曲子。}
# en: A warm castle bakehouse at midnight, a flour-dusted old baker kneading dough by the light of an open oven, a student leaning in the doorway.
scene [5fcd67] = 午夜里温暖的城堡烤房，一位满身面粉的老面包师借着敞开的炉火揉面，一个学生倚在门口。
# en: Knead until the oven's hot
opt.left.label [f28ed8] = 揉面直到炉子烧热
# en: {You knead until your arms shake. She gives you the first roll out of the oven and no lecture at all.|An hour of flour and warmth, and a hot roll for your trouble. You go back to bed with your hands smelling of bread, and sleep like a stone.|You knead while she hums something old. When the loaves go in, she toasts yesterday's heel for you, and you eat it on the step.}
opt.left.say.1 [1c4c8b] = {你揉面揉到胳膊发抖。她把第一个出炉的小面包给了你，一句说教也没有。|一个钟头的面粉和温暖，还有一个热乎乎的小面包作为酬劳。你回去睡觉时手上还带着面包味，睡得像块石头。|她哼着一支老歌，你揉着面。面包进炉后，她把昨天的面包头烤了给你，你坐在台阶上吃了。}
# en: Just sit by the oven
opt.right.label [363883] = 就坐在炉边
# en: {You sit by the open oven with your knees pulled up. She works, talks to the dough, and lets you be.|You sit by the oven with a roll from the cooling tray while she works. She doesn't ask why you're up. You don't ask why she is.|You eat the heel of bread and warm your feet. Upstairs, the castle is cold; down here, it never is.}
opt.right.say.1 [efc83a] = {你抱着膝盖坐在敞开的炉边。她干她的活，跟面团说话，由你待着。|她干活，你拿着晾盘上的一个小面包坐在炉边。她没问你为什么还醒着。你也没问她。|你吃了那块面包头，暖了暖脚。楼上的城堡很冷；这下面，从来不冷。}

@event restricted_page_buyer
# en: A Buyer for Old Pages
title [8c6109] = 古书页的买主
# en: {Grisk mentioned, once, that a collector pays for illuminated pages "of a certain age". The Restricted Section is full of them.|{flag(sold_page): There's a gap on the shelf where the last page you sold came from.|The illuminated book you read last time is back on its shelf, untouched.}|The illuminated books lean away from you as you pass.} {A gold-leaf dragon glints on one page.|One margin is full of tiny stars, all black.|A page here is worth a month's board.}
text [bb1bed] = {格里斯克曾提过一次，有个收藏家肯为“有些年头的”彩绘书页出钱。禁书区里满是这种书页。|{flag(sold_page): 书架上有个空缺，你上次卖的那一页就是从那儿来的。|你上次读过的那本彩绘书回到了书架上，原封未动。}|你经过时，那些彩绘书都往旁边躲。}{一页上有条金箔画的龙在闪光。|一处页边画满了小星星，全是黑的。|这里的一页抵得上一个月的食宿费。}
# en: A dim Restricted Section aisle at midnight, a student holding a razor over an illuminated page, a black book watching from the shelf above.
scene [84c409] = 午夜禁书区一条昏暗的过道，一个学生拿着刀片悬在一页彩绘书页上方，书架上一本黑书在看着。
# en: Cut a page
opt.left.label [5f6c23] = 割下一页
# en: {One clean cut. The book doesn't cry out, which is somehow worse. The collector pays well, and never asks where.|You sell the page and keep the guilt, which no one will buy.|The books lean away, and you cut a page anyway. A month's board, in one stroke. You don't come back to this aisle for a long time.}
opt.left.say.1 [c1c51f] = {干净利落的一刀。书没有叫出声，这不知怎么更糟。收藏家出价很高，也从不问来路。|你卖掉了书页，留下了愧疚，这东西没人肯买。|书都朝远离你的方向倾，你还是割了一页。一刀下去，一个月的食宿费。很长一段时间你都没再来这排书架。}
# en: Read it instead
opt.right.label [19ccdc] = 改为读它
# en: {You read the illuminated page by moonlight. It's a recipe for honey cakes, in exquisite gold leaf, and the gilding draws at your mana the whole time you read. You leave it where it is.|The page is a list of stars, by name, and each name pulls a little magic out of you as you read it. You learn three, and put the book back.|The books lean away from you, then back, as you read instead of cut. The page is a map of the castle as it was. It costs you a little magic to look at it.}
opt.right.say.1 [9d1c63] = {你借着月光读那页彩绘书页。是一份蜂蜜蛋糕的食谱，用精美的金箔写成，你读的时候那层金箔一直在吸你的魔力。你把它留在原处。|那一页是一份星星的名单，每个名字在你读出时都会从你身上抽走一点魔力。你记住了三颗，把书放了回去。|你读而不割，书先是朝外倾，后来又倾了回来。那一页是城堡从前的地图。看它要耗掉你一点魔力。}

@event midnight_roof_partner
# en: The Roof, Together
title [ad8b7c] = 屋顶上的两个人
# en: {You've brought {partner} up to the observatory roof, with a stolen blanket and two cups of cocoa going cold.|{partner} knows the way up now, and goes first.|{partner} has brought the blanket this time.} {The stars are very close.|A meteor, then another.|The castle below is all asleep.}
text [6b40c7] = {你把{partner}带上了观星台的屋顶，带着一条偷来的毯子和两杯渐渐变凉的可可。|{partner}现在认得上来的路了，走在前面。|这次是{partner}带了毯子。}{星星离得很近。|一颗流星，接着又是一颗。|下面的城堡全都睡着了。}
# en: Two students lying side by side on an observatory roof at midnight under a sky full of stars, one blanket between them.
scene [2af17c] = 午夜里两个学生并排躺在观星台屋顶上，头顶是满天星斗，两人盖着同一条毯子。
# en: Stay until the sky turns
opt.left.label [6b603a] = 待到天色变亮
# en: {You name the stars between you, wrong, and argue about it, and stay until the sky goes grey. The stair down is lit by a prefect's lamp you just avoid.|You fall asleep up there and wake to the first bell, frozen and happy.|{partner} wraps you both in the blanket {they} brought and talks you to sleep. The castle wakes up around you.}
opt.left.say.1 [bd9e3a] = {你们俩一起给星星起名字，起错了，争了起来，一直待到天色发灰。下楼时一位级长的灯光照亮了楼梯，你们刚好躲开。|你们在上面睡着了，醒来时第一遍钟已经响了，冻得要命，却很快乐。|{partner}用{them}带来的毯子把你们俩裹起来，说着话把你哄睡了。城堡在你们周围醒来。}
# en: An hour, then back
opt.right.label [3dda16] = 待一个钟头就回去
# en: {One hour, one blanket, back in bed before anyone stirs. You can still feel where {partner} was leaning on you.|You go down early. {partner} squeezes your hand on the stair, which is better than any star.|One hour under {partner}'s blanket. {They} fold{s} it and give{s} it to you at the bottom of the stair: "For next time."}
opt.right.say.1 [57c547] = {一个钟头，一条毯子，在任何人醒来前回到床上。你还能感觉到{partner}靠在你身上的地方。|你们早早下了楼。{partner}在楼梯上捏了捏你的手，比哪颗星星都好。|在{partner}的毯子底下待了一个钟头。在楼梯底下，{they}把毯子叠好递给你：“下次用。”}

@event kael_midnight_roof
# en: Kael at Midnight
title [c04a03] = 午夜的凯尔
# en: {Kael is on the observatory parapet, which he shouldn't be, with frost spreading from his fingers into the stone. He moves over to make room.|Kael again, on the parapet, the night's cold not touching him.|Kael has left room on the parapet before you arrive.} {"I can't sleep south of the mountains," he says. "Too warm."|He is watching the lake, not the stars.|"Northern stars," he says, pointing at nothing you can see.}
text [45cc53] = {凯尔坐在观星台的护墙上，这本来是不允许的，霜从他的指尖蔓延进石头里。他挪了挪，给你让出位置。|又是凯尔，坐在护墙上，夜里的寒气碰不到他。|你还没到，凯尔就已经在护墙上给你留好了位置。}{“在山脉以南我睡不着，”他说，“太暖和了。”|他在看湖，不在看星星。|“北方的星星，”他说着，指向一处你什么也看不见的地方。}
# en: A northern student sitting on the observatory parapet at midnight with frost spreading from his hands, the lake far below, the sky thick with stars.
scene [330d76] = 午夜里一个北方学生坐在观星台护墙上，霜从他手上蔓延开来，湖在远远的下方，天上星斗密布。
# en: Sit with him
opt.left.label [6fadbf] = 陪他坐一会儿
# en: {You sit until your fingers ache from the cold. He names northern constellations in a language that sounds like snow falling. It's the most he's ever said.|He doesn't talk. Neither do you. When you go, he says "Goodnight," as if it were difficult, and it was.|He's left room, so you take it. He points out a northern star you can't see, and you pretend you can. He knows, and is pleased.}
opt.left.say.1 [c3f2b3] = {你一直坐到手指冻得发疼。他用一种听起来像落雪的语言说出北方星座的名字。这是他说话最多的一次。|他不说话。你也不说。你走的时候，他说“晚安”，好像这很难说出口，确实如此。|他留了位置，你就坐了。他指着一颗你看不见的北方的星，你假装看见了。他知道，还挺高兴。}
# en: Ask what he's watching for
opt.right.label [442add] = 问他在等什么
# en: {"For it to wake," he says, and then shuts up like a book. You've pressed too hard. But you know which way he faces now.|"Nothing," he says, too fast. He's watching the middle of the lake. You leave him to it, colder than when you came.|"Home," he says, about the northern stars, and nothing more. It's the most honest thing he's told you, and he looks away after.}
opt.right.say.1 [085545] = {“等它醒来，”他说完，就像一本书一样合上了。你逼得太紧了。但现在你知道他面朝哪个方向了。|“没什么，”他说得太快。他在盯着湖中央。你留他一个人在那儿，走时比来时更冷。|“家，”他指着北方的星星说，再没多说。这是他对你说过最坦白的话，说完他移开了目光。}

@event corvin_note_was_mine
# en: Second Timetable
title [4a5d2a] = 第二张作息表
# en: In the gargoyle passage, Corvin holds up a map no bigger than a thumbnail. "Recognise it? The castle has a second timetable. It starts at midnight." He grins. "Who did you think writes notes like that? Prefects?"
text [2e7f05] = 在石像鬼通道里，科尔文举起一张不比拇指大的地图。“认得吗？城堡有第二张作息表。从午夜开始。”他咧嘴一笑。“你以为是谁写那种字条的？级长吗？”
# en: A secret passage behind a gargoyle at midnight, a grinning dark-haired student holding up a thumbnail-sized silver map, chalk marks on the wall behind him.
scene [35de3d] = 午夜一条石像鬼后面的秘密通道，一个咧嘴笑着的黑发学生举着一张拇指大小的银色地图，身后墙上画着粉笔记号。
# en: "Why me?"
opt.left.label [e79264] = “为什么是我？”
# en: "Because you looked at that door at the back of the library the way I do." He shrugs, and doesn't joke. "And because it's lonely, knowing all the doors." You don't sleep much, after.
opt.left.say.1 [b6a5ed] = “因为你看图书馆后面那扇门的眼神，跟我一样。”他耸耸肩，没有开玩笑。“还因为，知道所有的门，挺孤单的。”那之后你没怎么睡着。
# en: "You could have signed it."
opt.right.label [e5208c] = “你本可以署名的。”
# en: "And spoil it?" He tucks the map into your pocket. "Keep it. The doors move. The map knows." You check it in the morning, and one of the six doors has moved.
opt.right.say.1 [0b70cd] = “那多没意思？”他把地图塞进你口袋。“留着吧。门会挪地方。地图知道。”第二天早上你一看，六扇门里有一扇挪了位置。

@event corvin_midnight_watch
# en: Corvin Keeps Watch
title [aa7961] = 科尔文放风
# en: {Corvin leans out of a niche as you pass. "Bram's on the east stair. Take the west. You owe me nothing, I'm a saint."|Corvin's in his niche again with an apple and a list of where every prefect is.|"West stair," says Corvin, before you ask.} {He looks tired.|He has a new scratch on his cheek.|He's whistling, which he shouldn't.}
text [45e683] = {你经过时，科尔文从一个壁龛里探出身来。“布拉姆在东边楼梯。走西边。你什么都不欠我，我是圣人。”|科尔文又待在他的壁龛里，拿着一个苹果和一张每个级长的位置清单。|“西边楼梯，”你还没开口，科尔文就说了。}{他看起来很累。|他脸颊上多了一道新划痕。|他在吹口哨，这可不应该。}
# en: A dark corridor at midnight, a dark-haired student leaning out of a niche to wave someone past, a prefect's lantern turning a far corner.
scene [151b9a] = 午夜一条漆黑的走廊，一个黑发学生从壁龛里探出身来挥手让人通过，远处拐角有一盏级长的灯笼在转。
# en: Keep him company
opt.left.label [dd3cdd] = 陪他待一会儿
# en: {You share his apple and his niche. He tells you which tapestry hides a cupboard full of confiscated wands. You're up till the bells.|You keep watch with him for an hour. He's funnier at midnight, and sadder, and pretends to be neither.|He whistles until you shush him, then whistles quieter. You keep watch till the bell and learn three new routes.}
opt.left.say.1 [c9e2c9] = {你分享了他的苹果和他的壁龛。他告诉你哪块挂毯后面藏着一柜子没收来的魔杖。你一直待到钟声响起。|你陪他放了一个钟头的风。午夜的他更风趣，也更伤感，却假装两样都不是。|他一直吹口哨，你嘘了他，他就吹得小声些。你陪他守到钟响，学会了三条新路线。}
# en: Take the west stair
opt.right.label [19b545] = 走西边楼梯
# en: {The west stair is dark and empty, as promised. Corvin's map is never wrong. You wonder who taught him to be so careful.|You slip past Bram's lamp with a corridor to spare.|West stair, before you've asked. Corvin's whistling follows you down it, far too loud, and nobody catches either of you.}
opt.right.say.1 [f44f09] = {西边楼梯漆黑而空荡，正如他所说。科尔文的地图从来不会错。你很好奇是谁教会他这么小心的。|你隔着一条走廊的距离从布拉姆的灯下溜了过去。|你还没问他就说了西边楼梯。科尔文的口哨声一路跟着你下去，响得过分，可谁也没抓到你们俩。}

@event midnight_swim
# en: The Lake at Midnight
title [d7eddc] = 午夜的湖
# en: {season == "winter": The lake at midnight has a skin of ice at the edges and stars in the middle.|{~The lake at midnight is black and silver and perfectly still.|Nobody swims after curfew, which is why you do.|The water is warm from the day and the air is not.}} {clock(hollowstar) >= 5: Far out, a ring of frost forms and fades.|{~An owl crosses the moon.|Somewhere on the far shore, a lantern.|A fish jumps, very loudly.}}
text [aaf6ce] = {season == "winter": 午夜的湖边缘结了一层冰，中央倒映着星星。|{~午夜的湖黑中带银，纹丝不动。|宵禁后没人游泳，所以你才去。|水还留着白天的温度，空气却没有。}}{clock(hollowstar) >= 5: 远处，一圈霜冻成形，又消散了。|{~一只猫头鹰飞过月亮。|对岸某处有一盏灯笼。|一条鱼跳了起来，声音很响。}}
# en: A moonlit lakeshore at midnight, clothes folded on a rock, a swimmer's head and a ring of ripples in the silver water.
scene [7c16dd] = 午夜月光下的湖岸，衣服叠放在一块石头上，银色的水面上露出一个游泳者的头和一圈圈涟漪。
# en: Swim out to the middle
opt.left.label [1bcb3e] = 游到湖中央
# en: {~You swim until the castle is a toy and the stars are all around you. The cold gets into your bones and stays till breakfast.|You float on your back in the middle of the lake. Something far below hums, once. You swim back faster than you swam out.|You swim out and turn on your back. The stars and the water are the same colour, and you lose track of which is which. You swim back slowly.}
opt.left.say.1 [b1622d] = {~你一直游到城堡变得像个玩具，四面八方都是星星。寒气钻进骨头里，一直待到早饭时。|你仰面漂在湖中央。下面很深的地方嗡地响了一声。你游回去比游出来快多了。|你游出去，翻身仰躺。星星和湖水是同一种颜色，你分不清哪个是哪个。你慢慢地游了回去。}
# en: Paddle, then get dry
opt.right.label [cf2997] = 蹚蹚水就上岸擦干
# en: {~Knee-deep, then waist-deep, then out, gasping and laughing at yourself. Your teeth chatter all the way up the lawn.|A quick, cold paddle, and back to bed glowing.|You paddle until the fish jumps right beside you. You're out of the water before you've decided to be.}
opt.right.say.1 [04f629] = {~齐膝，齐腰，然后上岸，喘着气笑话自己。回草坪那头的一路上你的牙齿都在打颤。|又快又冷地蹚了一会儿水，回到床上浑身发热。|你蹚着水，直到那条鱼就在你身边跃起。你还没决定上岸，人已经在岸上了。}

@event grey_on_the_shore
# en: Someone Else Who Can't Sleep
title [cc0062] = 另一个睡不着的人
# en: The man in grey is sitting on an upturned boat at the water's edge, as if he'd been waiting for a ferry. "You can't sleep either," he says pleasantly. "Nobody sleeps well near this lake. Sit. I won't keep you long. I only want to tell you what the headmistress won't."
text [b8c4b5] = 灰衣人坐在水边一条倒扣的船上，像是在等渡船。“你也睡不着，”他愉快地说，“在这湖边没人睡得好。坐吧。我不会耽搁你太久。我只是想告诉你校长不肯说的事。”
# en: A moonlit lakeshore at midnight, a tall man in a grey coat sitting on an upturned boat, frost spreading from his boots across the pebbles.
scene [a47a73] = 午夜月光下的湖岸，一个穿灰大衣的高个男人坐在一条倒扣的船上，霜从他的靴子底下蔓延到卵石上。
# en: Sit and listen
opt.left.label [1a3cf5] = 坐下听他说
# en: He tells you, kindly, that the founders were frightened people who buried what they couldn't understand, and that it has been lonely down there for three hundred years. It sounds true. You walk back with it, and can't put it down.
opt.left.say.1 [7f0733] = 他和气地告诉你，创始者们是一群受了惊吓的人，把自己不理解的东西埋了起来，而那东西在下面已经孤单了三百年。听起来像是真的。你带着这些话走回去，怎么也放不下。
# en: Walk away
opt.right.label [96da1a] = 走开
# en: You turn your back and walk, and the cold follows you all the way up the lawn like a dog. At the door you look back. The boat is empty, and frosted white.
opt.right.say.1 [a9b029] = 你转身就走，寒意像条狗一样一路跟着你走过草坪。到了门口你回头一看，那条船空了，结满了白霜。
